1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Birth date estimated, depending on various sources, as anywhere c1225 to 1235).  Her marriage date is c1248 to c1250.
2 CONT
2 CONT Parents of Anastasia Pirovano not certain, although many sources state that the Archbishop Oberto II b1165 was her "uncle" (and perhaps actually her great uncle)
2 CONT
2 CONT These more "likely" sources have placed Anastasia's father as "Oberto", himself the son of an "unknown" Privano, brother of Oberto II Pirovano, Archbishop, both, along with Bertha, children of Andreotus Pirovano: http://gw.geneane
2 CONC t.org/richardclaude?lang=en&pz=genevieve+marcelle+juliette&nz=bedoussac&ocz=0&m=D&p=andreotus&n=pirovano&siblings=on&notes=on&t=T&v=6&image=on&marriage=on&full=on
2 CONT
2 CONT (Some sources state "a brother of Uberto", the Archibishop: http://fabpedigree.com/s045/f667321.htm This source states that Anastasia was the niece of Cardinal Uberto Pirovano, but primal source of her parents not known:  
2 CONT
2 CONT TIBALDO Visconti (-beheaded Gallarate 1276).  The Annales Mediolanenses record that "Archiepiscopum Ottonem…Tibaldi nepotis sui" was beheaded "in Galerate" in 1276[55].  m ANASTASIA Pirovano, niece of Cardinal Uberto Pirovano Arch
2 CONC bishop of Milan, daughter of --- (-1276, bur [Milan San Eustorgio]).  The primary source which confirms her parentage and marriage has not yet been identified.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Quoted from http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/MILAN.htm )
2 CONT ----
2 CONT http://gw.geneanet.org/jlcoupat?n=pirovano&oc=&p=andreotus
2 CONT
