1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Teobaldo Visconti'''
2 CONT
2 CONT "It was Teobaldo, son of Andreoccio, brother of Otto, by virtue of his value and by appearance of body, but much more for his happy offspring, very clear, because he left Matteo his son after him."  ( Paolo Giovio ) 
2 CONT * https://it.wikipedia.org/wiki/Teobaldo_(o_Tibaldo)_Visconti ('''Son of Andreotto''' 1853 source)
2 CONT * https://it.wikipedia.org/wiki/Visconti#Albero_genealogico '' /!\ (Son of Andreotto's BRO: Obizzo)'' 
2 CONT
2 CONT -----------
2 CONT
2 CONT *http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/MILAN.htm#_Toc359999140  '' /!\ (Son of  Obizzo)''
2 CONT
2 CONT a)         TIBALDO Visconti (-beheaded Gallarate 1276).  The Annales Mediolanenses record that "Archiepiscopum Ottonem…Tibaldi nepotis sui" was beheaded "in Galerate" in 1276[55].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' ANASTASIA Pirovano, niece of Cardinal Uberto Pirovano Archbishop of Milan, daughter of --- (-1276, bur [Milan San Eustorgio]).  The primary source which confirms her parentage and marriage has not yet been identified.   Ti
2 CONC baldo & his wife had [four] children:  
2 CONT
2 CONT ------------
2 CONT
2 CONT "A brother of Uberto", the Archibishop: http://fabpedigree.com/s045/f667321.htm This source states that his wife, Anastasia, was the niece of Cardinal Uberto Pirovano, but primal source of her parents not known:
2 CONT
2 CONT A soldier, TIBALDO Visconti was captured in battle. He was beheaded in Gallarate 1276 by Napo Torriani, along with 22 other prisoners <br/>
2 CONT (source https://it.wikipedia.org/wiki/Teobaldo_(o_Tibaldo)_Visconti ).  
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fabpedigree.com/s044/f667321.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT ------
2 CONT
2 CONT Figlio di Andreott0 o di Obizzo è '''Tebaldo''', che nel 1255 era rettore delle valli Levantina e di Blenio per lo zio Azzone, e fu il padre di Matteo;
2 CONT
2 CONT *https://www.treccani.it/enciclopedia/visconti_(Enciclopedia-Italiana)/
2 CONT
2 CONT ------
