1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Luchino_Visconti_%28died_1349%29 Wikipedia - '''Luchino Visconti'''] He co-ruled in Milan with his nephew Azzone Visconti and his brother Giovanni, until Azzones's death in 1339.
2 CONT
2 CONT Luchino was a patron of both music and literature.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married three times: to Violante of Saluzzo, then to Caterina Spomola, and in 1349 to Isabella Fiesci, niece of Pope Adrian V..
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------
2 CONT *https://www.treccani.it/enciclopedia/luchino-visconti_(Dizionario-di-Storia)/
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------
2 CONT
2 CONT -http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/MILAN.htm#LucchinoViscontidied1349<br/>
2 CONT 5.         LUCCHINO Visconti (-murdered Milan 24 Jan 1349, bur Milan, Crescentiaghi Church).  The Chronicon of Pietro Azario names "Galeaz primogenito, Johannes, Marcus, Luchinus et Stephanus" as the children of "Maphæolus…de Vice
2 CONC comitibus" and his wife "Dominam Violantam de Burris"[135].  The Chronicle of Matthias Nueweburgensis names "Goleaceo, Iohanne, Marco, Luca et Stephano" as the sons of "Matheo Mediolanensi domino"[136].  The Annales Mediolanenses 
2 CONC record the capture [5] Jul 1327 of "Galeazium Vicecomitem Dominum Civitatis et Azzonem filius eius et duo fratres ipsius Galeazii…Johannem Ordinarium Ecclesiæ Majoris et Luchinum" and their imprisonment "in castro de Modoëtia"[137
2 CONC ].  Lord of Milan 1339, jointly with his brothers.  "Johannes…episcopus Novariensis et comes…ac Luchinus fratres de Vicecomitibus, civitatis Mediolani…domini generales" confirmed concessions to the monastery of Chiaravalle by char
2 CONC ter dated 16 Sep 1339[138].  The Chronicon of Pietro Azario records the death 25 Jan 1348 (O.S.) of "Dominus Luchinus" and his burial "in ecclesia Crescentiaghi"[139].  Giovanni di Musso´s Chronicon Placentinum records the death 2
2 CONC 4 Jan 1348 of "Magnificus Dominus Luchinus Vicecomes civitatum Mediolani, Placentiæ, Parmæ, Cremonæ, Brixiæ, Pergami, Cumarum, Vercellarum, Novariæ, Terdonæ, Alexandriæ, Ast, Bobii, et Laudæ, nec non Castrorum Cremæ, Burgi S. Doni
2 CONC ni, et Pontremuli Dominus generalis"[140].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' firstly (1316) CATERINA Spinola, daughter of OBERTO Spinola Patrizio of Genoa & his wife --- (-1317).  The Chronicon of Pietro Azario records that "Luchinus…Vicecomes" married "uname de Spinolis"[141].  ...one child:
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' secondly ([1318]) ELISABETTA Fieschi, daughter of CARLO Fieschi Capitano of Genoa & his wife Teodora --- (-[after 1331 or after 1349]).  The Chronicon of Pietro Azario records that "Luchinus…Vicecomes" married "Dominam Eli
2 CONC sabetham de Flisco sororem…Domini Johannis de Flisco" after the death of his first wife[142].  Giovanni di Musso´s Chronicon Placentinum records the death in battle at "Parabiago in comitatu Mediolani" in 1337 of "Dominus Johannes
2 CONC  de Flisco de Janua…cuius sororem Dominus Luchinus duxerat in uxorem"[143].  The Annales Mediolanenses record that "Domina Elisabet de Flisco uxor…Domini Luchini" visited the church of San Marco in Venice in 1346 and that, after t
2 CONC he death of her husband, she fled Milan "cum filio suo parvulo Luchino novello" and settled in Genoa[144].  ... three children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT ['''m''' thirdly (1339) as her second husband, VIOLANTE di Saluzzo, widow of OBIZZO Spinola, daughter of TOMMASO I Marchese di Saluzzo & his wife Aloisia di Ceva.  The primary source which confirms her second marriage has not yet 
2 CONC been identified.   Secondary sources show Violante as the third wife of Lucchino and mother of his three younger legitimate children.  However, this inconsistent with the sources which record his wife Elisabetta as still alive whe
2 CONC n Lucchino was killed and as mother of his son Lucchino and also appears to be chronologically impossible.]  
2 CONT
2 CONT Lucchino had illegitimate children by unknown mistresses:  
