1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Jean De Vouthon's daughter, Isabelle/Ysabeau d'Arc, was the mother of Joan of Arc.  His spouse is not known with certainty. Some confusion surrounds two women with similar names, "Thadéa di Visconti" or "Thadée" as
2 CONC  well as one "spouse" named Marguerite Coln, who married a different "Jehan de Vouthon" (different birth dates). There may be a other homonyms. What seems MOST LIKELY, in view of all data seen:
2 CONT
2 CONT #  '''Thadea Valentina di Visconti (i.e. the Elder)''' married Jean de Vouthon, the ELDER (see this person's father), so is his '''mother''' (and not his wife, as some sites state).
2 CONT #  '''Thaddea de Visconti, the Younger''', neice of the above Thadea Valentina, N°1,  born in 1351 in Milan, married to a Bavarian prince, and mother of a future Queen Isabelle, wife of Charles VI of France (not the same 3 people)
2 CONC . This Bavarian princess passed away in Bavaria at around 30 yrs of age, in 1381.
