1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Son of the famous condottiere, Sir John Hawkwood of the "White Company", by Donnina (Domnina ) Visconti, whom he married in 1377. Returned to Essex after his fathers' death.
2 CONT
2 CONT Authorities. -M uratori, Rerum Italicarum scriptores, and supplement by Tartinius and Manni; Archivio storico italiano; TempleLeader and Marcotti, Giovanni Acuto (Florence, 1889; Eng. transl., Leader Scott, London, 1889); Nichol, 
2 CONC Bibliotheca topographica Britannica, vol. vi.; J. G. Alger in Register and Magazine of Biography, v. 1.; and article in Dict. Nat. Biog.
2 CONT
2 CONT Of his children by Donnina Visconti, who appears to have been his second wife, the eldest daughter married Count Brezaglia of Porciglia, podesta of Ferrara, who succeeded him as Florentine commander-in-chief, and another a German 
2 CONC condottiere named Conrad Prospergh. His son, John, returned to England and settled at Hedingham Sibil, where, it is supposed, Sir John Hawkwood was buried. The children of the first marriage were two sons and three daughters, and 
2 CONC of the latter the youngest married John Shelley, an ancestor of the poet.
2 CONT
