1 NOTE {geni:about_me} from [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Joan_of_France,_Duchess_of_Brittany '''Wikipedia'''], the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Joan of France''' (January 24, 1391 – September 27, 1433) was Duchess of Brittany through her marriage to John VI. She was a daughter of Charles VI of France and his wife, Isabeau of Bavaria.
2 CONT
2 CONT =Contents=
2 CONT
2 CONT * 1 Abduction of John VI by the Counts of Penthièvre
2 CONT * 2 Family
2 CONT * 3 Source
2 CONT
2 CONT =Abduction of John VI by the Counts of Penthièvre=
2 CONT
2 CONT The Counts of Penthièvre had lost the Breton War of Succession in the 1340s. As a result they lost the ducal title of Brittany to the Montforts. The conclusion to the conflict took many years to confirm until 1365 when the Treaty 
2 CONC of Guérande was signed. Despite the military loss and the diplomatic treaty, the Counts of Penthièvre had not renounced their ducal claims to Brittany and continued to pursue them.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1420 they invited John VI to a festival held at Châtonceaux. John came and was arrested. The Counts of Penthiève then spread rumours of his death and moved him to a new prison each day. Joan of France called upon all the barons
2 CONC  of Brittany to respond. They besieged all the castles of the Penthièvre family one by one.
2 CONT
2 CONT Joan ended by seizing the dowager countess of Penthièvre, Margaret of Clisson, forcing her to have the duke freed.
2 CONT
2 CONT =Family=
2 CONT
2 CONT Joan was mother to two Dukes of Brittany. She also had notable siblings.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1396 Joan married John VI, Duke of Brittany. Together they had seven children:
2 CONT
2 CONT * Anne (1409 – c. 1415)
2 CONT * Isabella (1411 – c. 1442), who in 1435 married Guy XIV of Laval and had 3 children with him.
2 CONT * Margaret (1412 – c. 1421)
2 CONT * Francis I (1414 – c. 1450), duke of Brittany
2 CONT * Catherine (1416 – c. 1421)
2 CONT * Peter II (1418 – c. 1457), duke of Brittany
2 CONT * Gilles (1420 – c. 1450), seigneur of Chantocé.
2 CONT
2 CONT Her most notable siblings were:
2 CONT
2 CONT * King Charles VII of France,
2 CONT * Catherine of Valois - she married King Henry V of England and was mother of King Henry VI of England),
2 CONT * Isabella of Valois - who married King Richard II of England, and
2 CONT * Michelle of Valois - she married Philip III, Duke of Burgundy.
2 CONT
2 CONT Joan died in 1433, during her husband's reign.
