2 CONT Charles VII, King of France 2     Charles VII, Roi de France was born on 22 February 1403 at Paris, France. He was the son of Charles VI, Roi de France and Isabelle von Bayern.3 He married Maria d'Anjou, daughter of Louis II, Duc 
2 CONC d'Anjou and Yolande de Aragón, on 18 December 1422. He died on 21 July 1461 at age 58 at Bourges, Orléanais, France. He was buried on 9 August 1461 at Saint-Denis, Île-de-France, France.
2 CONT      Charles VII, Roi de France was a member of the House of Valois.3 He and Agnès Sorel were associated.2 Charles VII, Roi de France also went by the nick-name of Charles 'The Victorious'.3 He succeeded to the title of Roi Charle
2 CONC s VII de France in 1422.3 Children of Charles VII, Roi de France and Maria d'Anjou 1.Louis XI, Roi de France+3 b. 3 Jul 1423, d. 30 Aug 1483 2.Jean de France2 b. 1424, d. 1425 3.Catherine de Valois1 b. 1428, d. 1446 4.Radegonde de
2 CONC  France2 b. 1428, d. 1444 5.Jacques de France2 b. 1432, d. 1437 6.Yolande de Valois b. 1434, d. 1478 7.Jeanne de Valois b. 1435, d. 1482 8.Marguerite de France2 b. 1437, d. 1438 9.Marie de France2 b. 7 Sep 1438, d. 14 Feb 1439 10.
2 CONC Jeanne de France2 b. 7 Sep 1438, d. 26 Dec 1446 11.Madeleine de Valois+ b. 1443, d. 1486 12.Charles de Valois, Duc de Berry et Guyenne b. 1446, d. 1472 Children of Charles VII, Roi de France and Agnès Sorel 1.Charlotte de Valois+2
