1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Jacqueline de Clermont (c. 1435–before 4 Sept 1482)
2 CONT Jacqueline de Clermont was a noblewoman of the Clermont family, active in the late 15th century in the region of Dordogne, Aquitaine, France. She was born around 1435 in Clermont, Dordogne, Aquitaine FamilySearch.org. Historical r
2 CONC ecords indicate she was the daughter of Hannes de Lohirville and Marie de Saint Martin FamilySearch.org.
2 CONT
2 CONT Family and Marriages
2 CONT Jacqueline was part of a prominent noble lineage. She married Arnould de Clermont (d. 1420) FamilySearch.org, though this early marriage appears to be a family connection rather than a personal union. Later, she married Doem de Cl
2 CONC ermont, who served as echevin de Liège, de Jupille et de Saive FamilySearch.org. She also married Jehan de Clermont (d. 1426) FamilySearch.org.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT Jacqueline had several children, including:
2 CONT
2 CONT Jutgen de Clermont (d. 1432)
2 CONT Herman or Jacques de Couves (d. 1508)
2 CONT Marie de Clermont (d. 1482)
2 CONT Jean de Clermont (d. 1446) 
2 CONT Jacques de Clermont (d. 1508) 
2 CONT Death
2 CONT She died before 4 September 1482
