1 NOTE {geni:about_me} According to Christian Wolff, Les Ancêtres d'Albert Schweitzer (Strasbourg (5, rue Fischart, 67000) : Publications du C.G.A., 1978)., Elsabeth Lyher (born between 1442-1443 and died 1490) is the daughter of [http:
2 CONC //www.geni.com/people/Chancellor-Konrad-Lyher/6000000000269766442 Chancellor Konrad Lyher] and [http://www.geni.com/people/Elisabeth-Von-Dagersheim/6000000000269766458?through=6000000000269766442 Elisabeth von Dagersheim].  She is
2 CONC  listed as
2 CONT *29241. Elisabeth LYHER, * 1442/43, x 1490, institua 1483 la fondation Volland ; mère d'Ambrosius Volland, célèbre chancelier wurtembergeois et féroce adversaire du n° 29244
2 CONT
2 CONT Her parents are listed as:
2 CONT *58482. Conrad LYHER, * Nurtingen v. 1410/15, x 1466/74 secrétaire privé d'Ulric le Bien Aimé comte de Wurtemberg à Stuttgart 1444-51, Vogt de Markgr. 1451-63, inféodé à Cannstatt, etc acheta le château de Rohrau ; oo av. 1443
2 CONT *48453. (Elisabeth ou Antonia) von DAGERSHEIM, *v. 1415, x ap. 1476, fille illégitime
2 CONT
2 CONT I understand that there may be some discrepancies on relationships in this branch.  [http://gw.geneanet.org/emig?lang=en;pz=christian+charles+theodore;nz=emig;ocz=0;p=elisabeth;n=lyher Christian Emig's tree] on Geneanet does not l
2 CONC ist a mother and does not list anything earlier than her father Conrad Lyher.  
2 CONT
2 CONT I have been in touch with Christian Emig and he said that some of Christian Wolff's work was shown to be incorrect later.  I will detach Elizabeth Lyher from the [http://www.geni.com/people/Elisabeth-Von-Dagersheim/600000000026976
2 CONC 6458 Elisabeth von Dagersheim] and the father since it seems this may have been based on some incorrect information or assumptions.
2 CONT
