1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://genealogics.org/getperson.php?personID=I00005683&tree=LEO
2 CONT
2 CONT Francis I, Duke of Brittany
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Francis I (in breton Fransez I, in french François I) (Vannes/Gwened, May 14, 1414 – July 18, 1450, Château de l'Hermine/Kastell an Erminig), was duke of Brittany, count of Montfort and titular earl of Richmond, from 1442 to his d
2 CONC eath. He was son of Duke John VI and Jeanne de Valois, princess of France.
2 CONT
2 CONT He first married, at Nantes in 1431, Yolande of Anjou (d. 1440), daughter of Louis II of Anjou. He was married again at the Château d'Auray on October 30, 1442, to Isabel of Scotland (daughter of James I, King of Scots) and had tw
2 CONC o daughters:
2 CONT
2 CONT Marguerite of Brittany (1443–1469, Nantes), married Francis II, Duke of Brittany
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary of Brittany (1444–1506), married John II, viscount of Rohan and count of Porhoët
2 CONT
2 CONT He was succeeded by his brother Peter.
