1 NOTE {geni:about_me} from [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marie_de_Valois '''Wikipedia'''], the free encyclopedia.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Marie Marguerite de Valois''' (1444–1473) was the natural daughter of King Charles VII of France and his mistress Agnès Sorel.
2 CONT
2 CONT She had two sisters, Charlotte de Valois (1446–1477) and Jeanne de Valois (born 1448).
2 CONT
2 CONT Marie married Olivier de Coétivy, Count of Taillebourg. Her older sister Charlotte married Jacques de Brézé, Count of Maulevrier, and mothered Louis de Brézé, seigneur d'Anet, husband of Diane de Poitiers. Allegedly Charlotte was 
2 CONC killed by her husband for having committed adultery.[1] Jeanne married Antoine de Bueil, Count of Sancerre.
2 CONT
2 CONT =Notes=
2 CONT * [http://www.heraldica.org/topics/france/roygenea.htm#bastards The French Royal Family: A Genealogy]
