2 CONT Renée de France[1] (25 October 1510 – 12 June 1574[2]) was the younger daughter of Louis XII of France and Anne, Duchess of Brittany. Her elder sister was Queen Claude of France. She was the Duchess of Ferrara due to her marriage 
2 CONC to Ercole II d'Este, grandson of Pope Alexander VI.
