1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Francesco_II_Sforza
2 CONT
2 CONT Francesco II Sforza (February 4, 1495 – October 24, 1535), also known as Francesco Maria Sforza[1], was the last Duke of Milan from 1521[2] until his death.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the son of Ludovico Sforza and Beatrice d'Este. When Ludovico was ousted from Milan in the course of the Italian Wars, he brought Francesco with him to the court of the Emperor Maximilian I, who had married a Sforza, France
2 CONC sco's cousin Bianca Maria. Francesco was assigned to an ecclesiastical career. His father was imprisoned and killed in 1508, but when Charles V re-conquered Milan from the French (1525), Francesco was appointed its duke, the last 
2 CONC of the family to hold that title.
2 CONT
2 CONT He returned to his state, depleted by twenty years of combat, promoting a cultural and economic recovery. In 1526 he adhered to the second Holy League with Francis I of France, Pope Clement VII and the Republic of Florence, and wa
2 CONC s besieged in the Castello Sforzesco
2 CONT
2 CONT On May 4, 1534 he married Christina of Denmark, daughter of Christian II of Denmark and Norway and Isabella of Burgundy.
2 CONT
2 CONT He fought at the Battle of Bicocca, and joined the League of Cognac against Charles V. His childless death in 1535 sparked the Italian War of 1535. His half-brother Giovanni Paolo reclaimed briefly the Duchy of Milan after his dea
2 CONC th, but died in the same year under mysterious circumstances.
