2 CONT
2 CONT Archduchess Margaret of Austria
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Jump to:navigation, search
2 CONT
2 CONT For other people named Margaret of Austria, see Margaret of Austria (disambiguation).
2 CONT
2 CONT Archduchess Margaret of Austria
2 CONT
2 CONT Princess of Asturias
2 CONT
2 CONT Duchess consort of Savoy
2 CONT
2 CONT Portrait of Margaret of Austria, dressed as a widow, by Bernard van Orley
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouse 	John, Prince of Asturias
2 CONT
2 CONT Philibert II, Duke of Savoy
2 CONT
2 CONT Father 	Maximilian I, Holy Roman Emperor
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother 	Mary, Duchess of Burgundy
2 CONT
2 CONT Born 	10 January 1480(1480-01-10)
2 CONT
2 CONT Died 	1 December 1530 (aged 50)
2 CONT
2 CONT Belgium
2 CONT
2 CONT Archduchess Margaret of Austria (German: Margaretha) (10 January 1480 – 1 December 1530) was the Governor of the Habsburg Netherlands (Landvogt) from 1507 to 1515 and from 1519 to 1530. She was the daughter of Maximilian I, Holy R
2 CONC oman Emperor, and Mary, Duchess of Burgundy.
2 CONT
2 CONT Contents
2 CONT
2 CONT [hide]
2 CONT
2 CONT     * 1 Early life
2 CONT
2 CONT     * 2 Marriages
2 CONT
2 CONT           o 2.1 First Marriage
2 CONT
2 CONT           o 2.2 Second Marriage
2 CONT
2 CONT     * 3 Political Role
