2 CONT Chancery pleadings<br>
2 CONT Peter Watson, of London, draper, and William Sybson, husband of Ellen, late the wife of William Gardyner v the Mayor, Aldermen, and Sheriffs of London: an action by the children of William Gardyner, deceased, to recover the portio
2 CONC n of his son Thomas, who has entered Westminster abbey. (C 1/252/12, dated 1501-1502, [http://discovery.nationalarchives.gov.uk/details/r/C7462868 The National Archives, Kew])
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Ellen, Elyn, or Helen Tudor''' (c.1459-after 1502).
2 CONT
2 CONT '''She and her husband William Gardiner were not the parents of [http://www.geni.com/people/Stephen-Gardiner/6000000003300420206?through=6000000029265451745 Stephen Gardiner,] Bishop of Winchester (d.1555), or Richard (1486-1546),
2 CONC  William (1488-1549) or Alice (d.1588) Gardiner.''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT *'''Helen Tudor1 
2 CONT *'''F, #107543, b. before 1467
2 CONT *Last Edited=5 Mar 2009
