1 NOTE He was elected to succeed his deposed nephew, Christian II. Owing his 
2 CONT throne to the nobles, Frederick granted them many privileges, thereby 
2 CONT diminishing the royal power. A sympathizer of Lutheranism, he facilitated 
2 CONT the spread of that faith in his dominions.
