1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John,_Elector_of_Saxony
2 CONT
2 CONT Issue
2 CONT Detail	Johann Frederick I, Elector of Saxony
2 CONT Maria, Duchess of Pomerania
2 CONT John Ernest, Duke of Saxe-Coburg
2 CONT House	House of Wettin
2 CONT Father	Ernest, Elector of Saxony
2 CONT Mother	Elisabeth of Bavaria
2 CONT
2 CONT Born in Meissen, John was the fifth of the seven children of Ernest, Elector of Saxony and Elisabeth of Bavaria. From 1486 onward he was the heir presumptive of his childless brother Frederick the Wise. John received a part of the
2 CONC  paternal inheritance and afterwards assisted his kinsman, Maximilian I, Holy Roman Emperor, in several campaigns. On his brother's death in 1525 John inherited the title of elector and as an early adherent of Luther was soon prom
2 CONC inent among Protestant reformers.[1] As his nickname "The Steadfast" indicates, he resolutely continued the policies of his brother toward protecting the progress of the Protestant Reformation.
