1 NAME Adrien de Pisseleu, seigneur d'Heilly
1 SEX M
1 DEAT
2 DATE 8 FEB 1558
2 ADDR
3 CITY Amiens
3 STAE Picardy
3 CTRY France
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://genealogics.org/getperson.php?personID=I00311560&tree=LEO
2 CONT
2 CONT BIOGRAPHY Adrien was the son of Guillaume de Pisseleu, seigneur d'Heilly, and his first wife Isabeau de Josne dite de Contay. He was lord of Heilly, Fontaine-Lavagnan, Ondeuil-le-Châtel and Bailieul-sur-Thérin, écuyer du roi, and 
2 CONC bailli, governor of Hesdin, captain of 1000 foot soldiers of the Legion of Picardy. Governor of Maubeuge in 1534, he was wounded in the capture of the town of Hesdin in 1537. 
2 CONT
2 CONT With his wife Charlotte d'Ailly, daughter of Louis d'Ailly, seigneur de Varennes, and Charlotte de Bournonville, he had three children of whom Jean and Anne Jeanne would have progeny. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Adrien died at Amiens on 8 February 1558 on his return from the prisons of the Holy Roman Empire. His widow erected a tomb of black marble for him in the choir of the church of Saint-Michel-Archange in the convent of the Minimes i
2 CONC n Amiens. His remains and those of other members of the Pisseleu family were disinterred from the church in the 18th century.
