1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Ercole II d'Este, Duke of Ferrara
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ercole_II_d%27Este
2 CONT
2 CONT Ercole II d'Este (5 April 1508 - 3 October 1559) was Duke of Ferrara, Modena and Reggio from 1534 to 1559. He was a member of the house of Este and the eldest son of Alfonso I d'Este and Lucrezia Borgia.
2 CONT
2 CONT Through his mother, Ercole was a grandson of Pope Alexander VI, nephew of Cesare Borgia, and cousin of Saint Francis Borgia. Through his father, he was nephew of both Isabella d'Este, "the First Lady of the Renaissance", and Cardi
2 CONC nal Ippolito d'Este.
2 CONT
2 CONT His siblings included Ippolito II, Archbishop of Milan and later Cardinal, nun Leonora, and Francesco, Marchese di Massalombarda. His half-siblings included Rodrigo Borgia of Aragon, Lucrezia’s son by Alfonso of Aragon, Duke of Bi
2 CONC sceglie, and perhaps Giovanni Borgia, the “infans Romanus”.
2 CONT
2 CONT In April 1528, he married Renée of France, the second daughter of Louis XII, King of France, and Anne of Brittany. Renée received from Francis I of France an ample dowry and annuity. Thus the court she assembled about her in Ferra
2 CONC ra corresponded to the tradition which the cultivation of science and art implicitly required, including scholars like Bernardo Tasso and Fulvio Pellegrini Morato.
2 CONT
2 CONT Their first child, Anna, born in 1531, who was married to Francis, Duke of Guise, was followed by Alfonso in 1533; Lucrezia in 1535, who was married to the Duke of Urbino Francesco Maria II della Rovere; and later Eleonora and Lui
2 CONC gi, whose education she carefully directed.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Ercole II d'Este, Duca di Ferrara (1)
2 CONT
2 CONT M, #107531, b. 5 April 1508, d. 3 October 1559
2 CONT
2 CONT Last Edited=19 Jan 2009
2 CONT
2 CONT      Ercole II d'Este, Duca di Ferrara was born on 5 April 1508.3,2 He was the son of Alfonso I d'Este, Duca di Ferrara and Lucrezia Borgia.1,2 He married Renée de Valois, daughter of Louis XII, Roi de France and Anne de Dreux, Du
2 CONC chesse de Bretagne, in 1528.3 He died on 3 October 1559 at age 51.3,2
2 CONT
2 CONT      Ercole II d'Este, Duca di Ferrara succeeded to the title of Duca di Ferrara in 1534.1
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Ercole II d'Este, Duca di Ferrara and Renée de Valois
2 CONT
2 CONT -1. Alfonso II d'Este, Duca di Ferrara1 d. 1597
2 CONT
2 CONT -2. Anna d'Este+4 b. 1531, d. 1607
