1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Louise de Montmorency==
2 CONT '''Louise de Montmorency (1496–1547) was a French noblewoman from the ancient House of Montmorency.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''She was the younger sister''' of Anne de Montmorency, Constable of France, '''and the mother''' of Gaspard de Coligny, Admiral of France.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Louise married her first husband, Ferri de Mailly, in 1511.[1] This marriage produced a daughter''', Madeleine de Mailly. Ferry died in 1513, and '''Louise remarried in 1514 to Gaspard I de Coligny. From her second marriage she
2 CONC  had three sons, all of whom played important roles in the first period of the French Wars of Religion''': Odet, Cardinal de Châtillon; Gaspard, the Admiral; and François, Seigneur d'Andelot.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''She had considerable patronage power independently of her husband,[2][3] and had an important role in spreading the influence of Calvinism in France in the 16th Century.[4]
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes
2 CONT * 1.^ [1]
2 CONT * 2.^ "The patronage power of early modern French noblewomen" by Sharon Kettering. The Historical Journal, Vol. 32, No. 4 (Dec., 1989), pp. 817-841 JSTOR
2 CONT * 3.^ "The Montmorencys and the Abbey of Sainte Trinité, Caen: Politics, Profit and Reform" by Joan Davies The Journal of Ecclesiastical History (2002), 53 : 665-685 doi:10.1017/S002204690200427X
2 CONT * 4.^ "The Development of Protestantism in 16th Century France" by Graham Noble; History Review, 2002 Questia link
2 CONT
2 CONT From: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Louise_de_Montmorency
2 CONT
2 CONT _______________________
2 CONT *'''Louise de Montmorency1
2 CONT *'''F, #81539, b. circa 1485, d. 22 June 1541
2 CONT *Father	William de Montmorency, Baron de Montmorency, d'Ecouen, Chantilly, & Damville1 d. 24 May 1531
2 CONT *Mother	Anne Pot2 d. 24 Feb 1510
2 CONT *'''     Louise de Montmorency was born circa 1485 at France.3 She married Ferry II de Mailly, Seigneur de Conty''', son of Adrien de Mailly and Jeanne de Berghes, '''circa 1504.3 A contract for the marriage of Louise de Montmoren
2 CONC cy and Gaspard I, Seigneur de Coligny, d'Andelot, & Chatillon sur Loing was signed on 1 December 1514.1 Louise de Montmorency married Gaspard I, Seigneur de Coligny, d'Andelot, & Chatillon sur Loing''', son of Jean III, Seigneur d
2 CONC e Coligny & Chatillon sur Loing and Eleonore de Courcelles, '''on 6 December 1514.1 Louise de Montmorency died on 22 June 1541 at Paris, Ile-de-France, France; Buried at Chatillon sur Loing.1,2
2 CONT *'''Family 1     Ferry II de Mailly, Seigneur de Conty b. c 1478, d. 1512
2 CONT *Child	
2 CONT **Madeleine de Mailly+3 b. c 1507, d. c 1570
2 CONT *'''Family 2     Gaspard I, Seigneur de Coligny, d'Andelot, & Chatillon sur Loing d. 24 Aug 1522
2 CONT *Child	
2 CONT **Gaspard II, Comte de Coligny, Admiral of France+1 b. 16 Feb 1517, d. 24 Aug 1572
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT *[S11569] Europaische Stammtafeln, by Wilhelm Karl, Prinz zu Isenburg, Vol. XIV, Tafel 61.
2 CONT *[S11569] Europaische Stammtafeln, by Wilhelm Karl, Prinz zu Isenburg, Vol. XIV, Tafel 130.
2 CONT *[S59] GeneaNet, Gérard DuPond de la Marteloye de Cercamp site.
2 CONT *From: http://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p2714.htm#i81539 __________________
2 CONT *'''The Love-affairs of the Condés: (1530-1740)      By Hugh Noel Williams
2 CONT *https://books.google.com/books?id=NlgoAAAAYAAJ&pg=PA7&lpg=PA7&dq=louise+montmorency+1550+mailly&source=bl&ots=djsdr1W3z1&sig=5G_bgew8cO3-uujYIQhrttHIZOs&hl=en&sa=X&ved=0CDYQ6AEwB2oVChMI7tGv0pXAxwIVTZmICh16qQeP#v=onepage&q=louise%
2 CONC 20montmorency%201550%20mailly&f=false
2 CONT *Pg.7
2 CONT * .... For Éléonore de Roye's mother, Madeleine de Mailly, was the '''daughter of Louise de Montmorency''', sister of the Constable;1 and '''Louise de Montmorency, by her second marriage with the Maréchal de Châtillon, was the mot
2 CONC her of the future Admiral''', Gaspard de Coligny, '''and of his two brothers''', Odet, Cardinal de Châtillon, and François, Seigneur d'Andelot.
2 CONT *   .... etc.
2 CONT **	1 '''By her marriage with Fery II. de Mailly, Baron de Conty. _________________
2 CONT *'''Littell's Living Age, Volume 188      edited by Eliakim Littell, Robert S. Littell
2 CONT *https://books.google.com/books?id=IC7WAAAAMAAJ&pg=PA580&lpg=PA580&dq=louise+montmorency+1550+mailly&source=bl&ots=WCEVwdIDT4&sig=JpSE0IXn51Seo6IWWMRJFGzxeak&hl=en&sa=X&ved=0CB0Q6AEwADgKahUKEwjn_sf2mMDHAhUJMIgKHSfhCoI#v=onepage&q=
2 CONC louise%20montmorency%201550%20mailly&f=false
2 CONT *Pg.580
2 CONT * .... Jacques II. was killed by the side of Bayard at the siege of Ravenna in 1512, and '''Gaspard I. inherited Châtillon. He married Louise de Montmorency''', the sister of the constable. He fought at Farnovo (1495), Agnadello  
2 CONC (1509), and Marignan (1515), and was made marshal of France in 1516. He died in 1522 at Dax, on his way to relieve Fontarabia. He was, says Brantôme, a man "du conseil duquel le roi s'est fort servi tant qu'il a vescu, comme il av
2 CONC ait raison, car il avait bone teste et bon bras." '''He left behind him three sons''' -- Odet de Châtillon, Cardinal Archbishop of Toulouse and Bishop of Beauvais; Gaspard II., born in 1517, Comte de Coligny, known in his youth as
2 CONC  Monsieur de Fromente, a castle now in ruins some four leagues from Bourg-en-Bresse; and François d'Andelot. '''The three boys were brought up by their mother, Louise de Montmorency.* Louise was twice married. By her first husband
2 CONC , the Comte de Mailly, she had a daughter''', Madeleine, afterwards Madame de Roye and mother-in-law of Louis de Bourbon, Prince de Condé. '''Louise de Montmorency was a firm, proud, austere, morally courageous woman.  ....  She d
2 CONC ied in 1547, refusing the aid of a priest.''' .... etc. __________________
2 CONT *'''La Belgique héraldique: recueil historique, chronologique ..., Volume 9     By Ch Poplimont
2 CONT *https://books.google.com/books?id=pnBWAAAAcAAJ&pg=PA337&lpg=PA337&dq=louise+montmorency+1550+mailly&source=bl&ots=SCbLWEcKgo&sig=rVQcwytt3YDtya-U4dSjtY4ypbU&hl=en&sa=X&ved=0CCYQ6AEwAzgKahUKEwjn_sf2mMDHAhUJMIgKHSfhCoI#v=onepage&q=
2 CONC louise%20montmorency%201550%20mailly&f=false
2 CONT *Pg.337
2 CONT *   XIV. CHARLES DE ROYE, sir de Roye, comte de Roucy, né le 14 janvier 1510, mort au château du Plessier de Roye, le 19 janvier 1551, épousa, le 27 août 1528, Madeleine de Mailly, '''fille de Ferry de Mailly, sire de Conty, et de
2 CONC  Louise de Montmorency''', cont trois enfants, savoir:
2 CONT **	A. .... etc. __________________
2 CONT *'''Généalogie de la famille de Roye, originaire de Picardie     By Fel. Vict Goethals
2 CONT *https://books.google.com/books?id=_RJTAAAAcAAJ&pg=PA20&lpg=PA20&dq=louise+montmorency+1550+mailly&source=bl&ots=fJrEB3gxUR&sig=SrjfvKjAhkNLLTmdVpvEq_gi9fI&hl=en&sa=X&ved=0CDIQ6AEwBTgKahUKEwjn_sf2mMDHAhUJMIgKHSfhCoI#v=onepage&q=lo
2 CONC uise%20montmorency%201550%20mailly&f=false
2 CONT *Pg.20
2 CONT *   XIV. Charles DE ROYE, sire de Roye, comte de Roucy, né le 14 janvier 1510, eut l'administration de toutes les terres données en douaire à la reine Éléonore, épousa, en présence du roi, à Saint-Germain-en-Laye, le 27 août 1528,
2 CONC  Madelaine de Mailly, '''fille et héritiére de Ferry de Mailly, sire de Conty, et de Louise de Montmorency''', qui en 1514, était remariée à Gaspard de Coligny, maréchal de France, et était sœur d'Anne, duc de Montmorency, premier
2 CONC  baron, pair, maréchal, grand-maitre et connétable de France. Charles DE ROYE mourut au château du Plessier de Roye le 19 janvier 1551; sa veuve lui survécut jusqu'en 1567. Ils sont enterrés en l'église de Muret. De ce Mariage son
2 CONC t issus:
2 CONT **	1 .... etc. __________________
2 CONT *'''Gaspard de Coligny : (Marquis de Chatillon), admiral of France, colonel of French infantry, governor of Picardy, Ile de France, Paris, and Havre (1879)   Author: Besant, Walter, Sir, 1836-1901
2 CONT *http://archive.org/details/gasparddecoligny00besauoft
2 CONT *http://archive.org/stream/gasparddecoligny00besauoft#page/26/mode/1up
2 CONT *''' .....  Louise de Montmorency, sister of the Constable, Anne de Montmorency, and widow of Frederic de Mailly, Baron of Conty, by whom she had one daughter, Madeleine.1 The Issue of her second marriage consisted of four boys--P
2 CONC ierre, Odet, Gaspard, and Francois. ..... _______________________________
2 CONT *'''Extrait de la généalogie de la maison de Mailly, dressé par m. ***      By Paul Lucas
2 CONT *https://books.google.com/books?id=acoOAAAAQAAJ&pg=PA207&lpg=PA207&dq=Jean+D%27+Mailly+1509&source=bl&ots=i6q5xpXvZI&sig=XxTw89OiEu679Y_5t1Kx9hSPCYs&hl=en&sa=X&ved=0CB0Q6AEwADgKahUKEwiEx7Kh0r_HAhVCK4gKHfUSD-c#v=onepage&q=hardouin&
2 CONC f=false
2 CONT *Pg.20
2 CONT * .... etc.
2 CONT **	(c) Par '''Ferry de Mailly qui époufa Louife de Montmorency''' Dame d'Honneur des Reines, Anne de Bretagne & Eleonor d'Autriche, fille de Guillame de Montmorency, premier Chambellan de France, fœur d'Anne Duc de Montmorency, Pa
2 CONC ir de France, premier Baron, dixiéme Connêrable & Grand Maître de France, Chevalier des Ordres de St. Michel & de la Jarretiere, tué à la Bataille de St. Denis en 1567. tante de François, Duc de Montmorency, Pair & Maréchal de Fra
2 CONC nce, Gouverneur de Paris, de Henry Duc de Damville, puis de Monmorency, Par & Maréchal de France, Gouverneur de Languedoc, & de Charles Duc de Damville, Pair & Amiral de France, mort en 1612.
2 CONT **	... etc.
2 CONT *Pg.21
2 CONT **	(c) Par Madeleine de Mailly, '''fille de Ferry, deuxiéme Baron de Conty''', mariée à St. Germain en Préfence du Roi, l'an 1528 avec Charles Sire de Roye Comte de Roucy fils d'Antoine Sire de Roye & de Catherine Sarrebrake Comte
2 CONC ffe de Montbelliard. De cette alliance vint Eleonore Dame de Roye, Baronne de Conty, qui eut l'honneur d'époufer Louis de Bourbon premier du nom, Prince de Condé, frere puîné d'Antoine de Bourbon Duc de Vendôme, Roi de Navarre, pe
2 CONC re d'Henri IV. Ainfi Madeleine de Mailly fe trouve grande tante de ce Monarque, arriere grande tante de Louis XIII. pere de Louis XIV. bifayeul d'un Prince qui fait l'objet de l'amour de fon peuple, comme celui de fon bonheur.
2 CONT **	.... etc. ________________________
