1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Madeleine of France (August 10, 1520 – July 2, 1537) was the daughter of Francis I of France and Claude of France. She was married to James V of Scotland on January 1, 1537 in Notre Dame Cathedral in Paris, France.
2 CONT
2 CONT Madeleine got sick with tuberculosis when she went to live in Scotland and died when she was only 16 years old. She is buried in Holyrood Abbey in Edinburgh, Scotland.
