2 CONT *'''   SHELLEY, SIR WILLIAM (1480?-1549?), judge, born about 1480, was the eldest son of Sir John Shelley (d. 3 Jan. 1526) and his wife Elizabeth (d. 31 July 1513), daughter and heir of John de Michelgrove in the parish of Clapham
2 CONC , Sussex (reproductions of monumental brasses in Addit. MS. 32490).''' .... etc.
2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/dictionarynatio01leegoog#page/n60/mode/1up
2 CONT *Pg.42
2 CONT * .... '''He died between 3 Nov. 1548 and 10 May 1549.'''
2 CONT *'''   Shelley married Alice (d. 1536?), daughter of Sir Henry Belknap, great-grandson of Sir Robert de Bealknap [q. v.] of Knelle in the parish of Beckley, Sussex. By her he had four sons:''' John (d. 15 Dec. 1550) was father of 
2 CONC William (not be confused with William Shelley of Hertford, also a prisoner in the Tower in 1580), who was attainted 15 Dec. 1582 for complicity in Charles Paget's treasons, but not executed, and died 15 April 1597, being succeeded
2 CONC  by his son John, created a baronet in 1611; the second son of the judge was Sir Richard Shelley [q. v.]; the third, Sir James, was, like Sir Richard, a distinquished and widely travelled knight of St. John (cf. Notes and Queries,
2 CONC  1st ser. viii. 192, x. 201-2); the fourth, Sir Edward, a master of the household of Henry VIII, treasurer of the council of the north, and captain of Berwick, was killed at Pinkie on 10 Sept. 1547 (cf. Addit. MSS. 32647 ff. 66, 7
2 CONC 0, 32648 f. 12, 32653 f. 161; Chron. of Calais, p. 176, &c.; Lit. Rem. of Edward VI, Rosb. Club, pp. cc; Cal. Hamilton Papers, passim). .... etc. _______________________
2 CONT *SHELLEY, Richard (1513/14-87).
2 CONT *b. 1513/14, '''3rd s. of (Sir) William Shelley of Michelgrove, Suss. by Alice, da. and event. coh. of Henry Belknap''' of Knell, Beckley, Suss. unm. Kntd. May 1555/Jan. 1557.1
2 CONT *From: http://www.historyofparliamentonline.org/volume/1509-1558/member/shelley-richard-151314-87 _________________________
2 CONT *COPLEY, Thomas (1532-84), of Gatton, Surr.
2 CONT *b. Feb./May 1532, o. s. of Sir Roger Copley of Gatton and Roughey, Suss. by 2nd w. Elizabeth, da. of '''(Sir) William Shelley of Michelgrove, Suss'''. educ. I. Temple, adm. 2 Nov. 1547. m. July 1558, Catherine, da. and coh. of Si
2 CONC r John Luttrell of Dunster, Som., 4s. 4da. suc. fa. 10 Sept. 1549.1
