1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ENRIQUE (II) titular King of Navarre, Comte de Foix et de Bigorre, Vicomte de Béarn et de Marsan, Duc de Nemours et de Montblanc (Sangüesa 18 Apr 1503-Hagetmau en Béarn, Landes 29 May 1555, bur Lescar Cathedral).
2 CONT x  MARGUERITE d'Orléans Dss de Berry
2 CONT *JUANA *JUAN 
2 CONT xx mistress
2 CONT JEAN Alespées 
2 CONT _________
2 CONT *''''''Henry II (18 April 1503 – 25 May 1555) was the eldest son of John III of Navarre (died 1516) and Catherine I of Navarre, sister and heiress of Francis Phoebus, King of Navarre; he was born at Sangüesa.
2 CONT *King of Navarre
2 CONT *''''''When Catherine died in exile in 1517, Henry was proclaimed king of Navarre. The title was also claimed by Ferdinand II of Aragon, who had invaded the realm in 1512. Under the protection of King François I of France, he assu
2 CONC med the title of King of Navarre and was lavishly crowned in Lescar, despite Ferdinand's claim being continued by his grandson Charles I.
2 CONT *''''''After ineffectual conferences at Noyon in 1516 and at Montpellier in 1518, an active effort was made in 1521 to establish him in de facto sovereignty. The French and Navarrese invaded Spanish Navarre, but were ultimately ex
2 CONC pelled by Charles I forces after the Battle of Noain (June 1521).
2 CONT *''''''In 1525, Henry was taken prisoner at the Battle of Pavia, but he contrived to escape under a guise and in 1526, married Marguerite, sister of King François I and widow of Charles, Duke of Alençon. By her, he was the father 
2 CONC of Jeanne d'Albret, and was consequently the grandfather of Henry IV of France. Henry, who had some strong sympathy with the Huguenots, died at Pau on 25 May 1555.
2 CONT *Marriage
2 CONT *''''''In 1526, he married Marguerite de Valois[1] who became known as Marguerite de Navarre (11 April 1492- 21 December 1549) and had issue:
2 CONT **1.Jeanne III of Navarre (16 November 1528–9 June 1572)
2 CONT **2.Jean (7 July 1530- 25 December 1530)
2 CONT etc.
2 CONT From: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Henry_II_of_Navarre
2 CONT _____________
2 CONT *''''''The Encyclopaedia Britannica
2 CONT *http://www.archive.org/stream/encyclopaediabri01chisrich#page/512/mode/1up
2 CONT *Pg. 512-513
2 CONT *ALBRET, the lordship (seigneueie) of Albret (Labrit, Lebret), situated in the Landes, gave its name to one of the most powerful feudal families of France in the middle ages. Its members distinguished themselves in the local wars 
2 CONC of that epoch; and during the 14th century they espoused the English cause for some time, afterwards transferring their support to the side of France. Arnaud Amanieu, lord of Albret, helped to take Guienne from the English. His so
2 CONC n Charles became constable of France and was killed at the battle of Agincourt in 1415. Alain the Great, lord of Albret (d. 1522), wished to marry Anne of Brittany, and to that end fought against Charles VIII.; but his hopes being
2 CONC  defeated by the betrothal of Anne to Maximilian of Austria, he surrendered Nantes to the Franch in 1486. At that time the house of Albret had attained considerable territorial importance, due in great part to the liberal grants w
2 CONC hich it had obtained from successive kings of France. John of Albret, son of Alain, became king of Navarre by his marriage with Catherine of Foix. Their son ''''''Henry, king of Navarre, was created duke of Albret and peer of Fran
2 CONC ce in 1550. By his wife Margaret, sister of the French king, Francis I., he had a daughter'''''', Jeanne d'Albret, queen of Navarre, who married Anthony de Bourbon, Duke of Vendom, and became the mother of Henry IV., king of Franc
2 CONC e. The dukedom of Albret, united to the crown of France by the accession of this prince, was granted to the family of La Tour d'Auvergne in 1651, in exchange for Sedan and Raucourt.
2 CONT *	To a younger branch of this house belonged Jean d'Albert, seigneur of Orval, count of Dreux and of Rethel, governor of Champagne (d. 1524), who was employed by Francis I. in many diplomatic negotiations, more particularly in his
2 CONC  intrigues to get himself elected emperor in 1519. (M.P.*)
2 CONT ___________
2 CONT '''Henri II d' Albret, King of Navarre, Comte de Foix & Bigorre'''1
2 CONT Last Edited	20 Mar 2002
2 CONT M, #81442, '''b. 24 April 1503, d. 29 May 1555'''
2 CONT '''Father'''	Jean d' Albret, King of Navarre1 b. 1469, d. 17 Jun 1516
2 CONT '''Mother'''	Katharina de Foix, Queen of Navarre, Countess de Foix & Bigorre1 b. 1470, d. 12 Feb 1517
2 CONT '''     Henri II d' Albret, King of Navarre, Comte de Foix & Bigorre was born on 24 April 1503 at Sanguesa.1 He married Marguerite d' Orleans, Duchess d'Alencon & Berry''', daughter of Charles d' Orleans, Comte d'Angouleme & Perig
2 CONC ord and Louise de Savoy, '''on 24 January 1527 at St. Germaine en Laye.2 Henri II d' Albret, King of Navarre, Comte de Foix & Bigorre died on 29 May 1555 at Hagetmau at age 52; Buried at St. Germain en Laye.'''1
2 CONT '''Family'''
2 CONT '''Marguerite d' Orleans, Duchess d'Alencon & Berry''' b. 11 Apr 1492, d. 21 Dec 1549
2 CONT '''Child'''	
2 CONT *Jeanne III d' Albret Queen of Navarre, Princess of Bearn+1 b. 7 Jan 1528, d. 9 Jun 1572
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT 1.[S11569] Europaische Stammtafeln, by Wilhelm Karl, Prinz zu Isenburg, Vol. II, Tafel 14B.
2 CONT 2.[S11569] Europaische Stammtafeln, by Wilhelm Karl, Prinz zu Isenburg, Vol. II, Tafel 14B & 24.
