1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT As to the family name, I have gleaned the family name was 
2 CONT
2 CONT originally "von Buus," 
2 CONT
2 CONT indicating they are from the town of Buus, quickly changing to "Buser" to indicate the same connotation. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Following the 30 years war, the death of Hans "der Canis" Buser 
2 CONT
2 CONT Loss of title and lands forced the family to relocate to Palatine Germany where the name Buser was Germanized to Bausser. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Family history states the family of 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mathias Imm Bausser Sr. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Emigrated to Penn Colony for the sake of religious freedom, and upon arrival, the colonial immigration service Anglicized the name Bausser as Bowser, where the pronunciation shifted from the double S sound to a Z sound.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.familycentral.net/index/family.cfm?ref1=16165:2377&ref2=16165:2378
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Hans Buser - Anna Goetschi
2 CONT
2 CONT Hans Buser was born at of Ruemlingen, Basel, Switzerland Abt 1538.
2 CONT He married Anna Goetschi . Anna Goetschi was born at of Ruemlingen, Basel, Switzerland Abt 1542 daughter of Herman Goetschi and Barbara Seyfried .
2 CONT
2 CONT Hans Buser - Anna Goetschi
2 CONT
2 CONT Hans Buser was born at of Ruemlingen, Basel, Switzerland Abt 1538.
2 CONT He married Anna Goetschi . Anna Goetschi was born at of Ruemlingen, Basel, Switzerland Abt 1542 daughter of Herman Goetschi and Barbara Seyfried .
2 CONT
2 CONT They were the parents of 8 children:
2 CONT Matthis Buser born Abt 1565.
2 CONT Johannes Buser born Abt 1566.
2 CONT Agnes Buser born 14 Mar 1570.
2 CONT Heinrich Buser born 1575.
2 CONT Israel Buser born Mar 1577.
2 CONT Margaretha Buser born 11 Sep 1580.
2 CONT Jacob Buser born 18 Mar 1582.
2 CONT Anna Buser born 14 Jun 1584.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
