2 CONT https://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eleonore_von_W%C3%BCrttemberg
2 CONT
2 CONT Eleanor of Württemberg (* 22. Marches 1552 in Tübingen; † 12. Jan 1618 On Lichtenberg Castle, Fischbachtal, Hesse) was a princess of Wurttemberg And by marriage, Princess of Anhalt and Landgravine of Hesse(-Darmstadt). She gained 
2 CONC additional importance as a promoter of medicine.
2 CONT
2 CONT Life
2 CONT Eleonore was a daughter of the Duke Christophe of Wurttemberg (1515–1568) and the latter's wife Anna Maria of Brandenburg-Ansbach (1526–1589).
2 CONT
2 CONT When she was almost 19 years old, she was born on the 9th. January 1571 in Stuttgart with the widowed prince Joachim Ernst of Anhalt (1536–1586), who brought five children into the marriage. As a result Dessau in Principality of A
2 CONC nhalt alive, Eleonore gave birth to ten children.
2 CONT
2 CONT After her husband's death in 1586, she married on the 25th. May 1589 in Darmstadt the widowed landgrave George I. of Hesse-Darmstadt. During this seven-year union she gave birth to a son.
2 CONT
2 CONT Afterwards she lived at the Duke's court Frederick William I. of Saxe-Weimar, who was formerly married to her sister Sophie, but now with Anna Maria of Palatinate-Neuburg. Since 1591 the Duke held the office of administrator of El
2 CONC ectoral Saxony from; He also had his residence in Torgau taken.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kurf%C3%BCrstentum_Sachsen
2 CONT
2 CONT The Electorate of Saxony, briefly too Electoral Saxony Or Chursachsen, was a territory of the Holy Roman Empire.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1356 that became Duchy Saxe-Wittenberg through 
2 CONT
2 CONT Emperors Charles IV. in the Golden Bull to one of the Courland Appointed. 
2 CONT
2 CONT From then on they posed Ascanians an elector. After the Saxon-Wittenberg line of the Ascanians died out Male line 1422 enfeoffed 1423 
2 CONT
2 CONT Roman-German king Sigismund den Meissnian Margraves Frederick the Quarrelsome from the line of Wettiner with the duchy, 
2 CONT
2 CONT whereby the Saxon electoral dignity also passed to it in 1423. Due to the electorate of the ruler, the name was subsequently changed 
2 CONT
2 CONT Electorate of Saxony 
2 CONT
2 CONT also for them Meissnian And Thuringian Wettin possessions used, 
2 CONT
2 CONT although the electoral dignity was linked only to part of the electoral territories, the Courlands In the case of the Saxon Electorate, this was the 
2 CONT
2 CONT Spa circle, the area of the former Duchy of Saxony-Wittenberg.
2 CONT
2 CONT Im Treaty of Leipzig of 1485 was the division of the Wettin noble house into the Ernestine line And the Albertine Line Agreed
2 CONT
2 CONT Eleonore was very interested not only in medicine, but also in other areas of knowledge. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Under the pseudonym „Lobesan“, which means „pious, laudable“ in Old High German, 
2 CONT
2 CONT she wrote a house and recipe book about water with the support of the ducal personal physician and proofreader Rebhold, 
2 CONT
2 CONT Diseases of the body and limbs, diseases of women and children, surgery, confectionery and essences, with an instruction for proper use. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The book was printed by the Duke in 1594 Hartenfels Castle founded the 
2 CONT
2 CONT Princely Saxon Printing House in Torgaw, which printed 
2 CONT
2 CONT Protestant theological but also political writings. This must have happened before 1601.
2 CONT
2 CONT As part of the move of the 
2 CONT
2 CONT court of Duke Friedrich Wilhelm I in 1601 Weimar, 
2 CONT
2 CONT or after his death the following year, the princess apparently 
2 CONT
2 CONT returned Hessen back, where she died on her widow's estate in 1618.
2 CONT
2 CONT
