2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maria_Anna_of_Bavaria_%281551%E2%80%931608%29
2 CONT =Maria Anna of Bavaria (1551–1608)=
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT Jump to:navigation, search For other people named Maria Anna of Bavaria, see Maria Anna of Bavaria (disambiguation). Maria Anna of Bavaria Archduchess consort of Austria Tenure 	26 August 1571 – 10 July 1590 Spouse 	Charles II of 
2 CONC Austria Issue Anna, Queen of Poland Maria Christierna, Countess of Tyrol Ferdinand II, Holy Roman Emperor Margaret, Queen of Spain and Portugal Leopold V, Archduke of Austria Constance, Queen of Poland Maria Magdalena, Grand Duche
2 CONC ss of Tuscany House 	House of Wittelsbach (by birth) House of Habsburg(by marriage) Father 	Albert V, Duke of Bavaria Mother 	Anne of Austria Born 	21 March 1551 Munich, Germany Died 	29 April 1608 (aged 57) Graz, Austria
2 CONT
2 CONT Maria Anna of Bavaria (21 March 1551, Munich Germany-29 April 1608, Graz Austria)[1] was the daughter of Albert V, Duke of Bavaria (1528-1579) and Anna of Austria (1528-1590). Contents [show]
2 CONT
2 CONT     * 1 Family
2 CONT     * 2 Marriage and children
2 CONT     * 3 Gallery of Family
2 CONT     * 4 Ancestors
2 CONT     * 5 Bibliography
2 CONT     * 6 References
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit] Family
2 CONT
2 CONT Her paternal grandparents were William IV, Duke of Bavaria (1493-1550) and Maria Jacoba, Margravine of Baden (1507-1580). Her maternal grandparents were Ferdinand I, Holy Roman Emperor (1503-1564) and Anna of Bohemia and Hungary (
2 CONC 1503-1547), daughter of King Ladislaus II of Bohemia and Hungary and his wife Anne de Foix. King Louis XIV of France is her lineal descendant.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Maria Anna was the fourth of seven siblings, only five of the children lived through to adulthood. Maria Anna's siblings included: William V, Duke of Bavaria, Ernest of Bavaria, Ferdinand of Bavaria and her unmarried sister, Maxim
2 CONC iliana Maria of Bavaria (who once was appointed to marry king Sebastian of Portugal). [edit] Marriage and children
2 CONT
2 CONT On 26 August 1571 in Vienna Maria Anna married her maternal uncle, Charles II of Austria (1540-1590). At first the Duke was betrothed to Elizabeth I of England, but she refused to marry Charles.
2 CONT
2 CONT Within nineteen years of marriage, Charles and Maria Anna had fifteen children:
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Ferdinand (b./d. 1572)
2 CONT     * Anna of Austria (1573-1598), married in 1592 Sigismund III Vasa of Poland (1566-1632)
2 CONT     * Maria Christierna (1574-1621), married in 1595 Sigismund Báthory von Siebenburgen (1572-1613)
2 CONT     * Katharina (1576-1595)
2 CONT     * Elisabeth (1577-1586)
2 CONT     * Ferdinand II, Holy Roman Emperor (1578-1637), married in 1600 a younger Maria Anna of Bavaria (1574-1616) and in 1622 Eleonore Gonzaga (1598-1655)
2 CONT     * Karl (1579-1580)
2 CONT     * Gregoria (1581-1597)
2 CONT     * Eleonora (1582-1620)
2 CONT     * Maximilian (1583-1616)
2 CONT     * Margaret of Austria (1584-1611), married in 1599 Philip III of Spain (1578-1621). She was the mother of Anne of Austria, Queen Consort of France
2 CONT     * Leopold V of Austria (1586-1632), married in 1626 Claudia de' Medici (1604-1648)
2 CONT     * Constance of Austria (1588-1631), married in 1605 Sigismund III Vasa of Poland (1566-1632)
2 CONT     * Maria Magdalena (1589-1631), married in 1608 Cosimo II de' Medici, Grand Duke of Tuscany (1590-1621)
2 CONT     * Karl (1590-1624)
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit] Gallery of Family
