1 NOTE BIOGRAPHY: Became the leader of the Huguenots in 1569 upon the death of the Prince de Condé (Louis I de Bourbon).
2 CONT
2 CONT BIOGRAPHY: From Marcel Muise (http://www.uftree.com/UFT/WebPages/marcelm/PHILIPPE/i0000134.htm):
2 CONT
2 CONT BIOGRAPHY: Two years of peace between the Huguenots (Protestants) and Roman Catholics ended in 1572 with the massacre of thousands of Huguenots in Paris, known as the St. Bartholomew's Day Massacre. Admiral Coligny and other Hugue
2 CONC not leaders, in Paris for a wedding were betrayed by the Queen Mother, Catherine de Médicis. Coligny stayed in Paris that evening with five Swiss guards, a Mr. Labonne, Mr. Yolet (his Master of Horses), a half dozen servants, and
2 CONC  Nicolaus Mius (his German interpreter.) On the Queen's orders Cosseins (the Duke of Guisse), the Duke of Aumale, the bastard Angoulême, and a band of French and Italians went from the Louvre to Rue de Béthisy where Coligny was 
2 CONC staying. Labonne was killed when he answered at the gate and several servants were slain in the courtyard. The Suisse barricaded the door. Coligny urged his followers to escape. Only Nicolas Mius refused and stayed by his side. Th
2 CONC e Catholics broke through and hesitated before Cosseins ordered them to shoot their Suisse countrymen. Nicolaus Mius was killed upstairs at the door to Coligny`s chamber. The Admiral was was hit several times with a battle axe and
2 CONC  thrown from the window, landing at Guisse`s feet. Coligny`s body was mutilated at the scene, then dragged to the Seine, thrown in the river, dragged out and hung in chains upside down at the gibbet of Montfaucon. His head was all
2 CONC egedly sent to the Pope. His remains were removed later by servants and turned over to his daughter Louise, Princess of Orange in Holland. They were later laid to rest at the castle at Châtillon sur Loing.
