1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Louis_II,_Cardinal_of_Guise
2 CONT
2 CONT Louis II, Cardinal of Guise (6 July 1555, Dampierre – 24 December 1588, Château de Blois) was the third son of Francis, Duke of Guise and Anna d'Este. His maternal grandparents were Ercole d'Este II, Duke of Ferrara and Renée of F
2 CONC rance.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was elected archbishop of Reims in 1574, succeeding his uncle, Charles of Guise. On 21 February 1578, he was created cardinal; he took the title of Cardinal of Guise, succeeding his uncle Louis I, Cardinal of Guise. He was late
2 CONC r named papal legate to Avignon, and made by Henry III of France a knight of the Order of Saint Esprit.
2 CONT
2 CONT His dedication to the cause of his brother Henry I, Duke of Guise and intransigence to the royal power provoked the hostility of Henry III. At the royal command, the Cardinal was assassinated at the Château de Blois by the King's 
2 CONC bodyguard known as "the Forty-five", the day after his brother.
2 CONT
2 CONT An illegitimate son, Louis bâtard de Guise (1588 – 1631), born of his liaison with Aimerie de Lescheraine, dame de Grimaucourt, was legitimised in 1610, after his father's death.
