1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Anne-Catherine brought the pedigree of the House of Chabot—a family so closely linked to King Francis I that her father served as Admiral of France—providing the "Crown-Level Alliance" necessary for the Halluin fam
2 CONC ily’s ducal ascent.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''(Gen 16) Anne-Catherine d'Halluin (de Chabot-Brion); 1st Duchesse d’Halluin (by marriage); Dame de Maignelay'''
2 CONT
2 CONT The Consort of the Ducal Ascent
2 CONT
2 CONT '''I. Profile Data'''
2 CONT Full Name: Anne-Catherine de Chabot-Brion
2 CONT Generation: 16
2 CONT Status: 1st Duchesse d’Halluin (by marriage); Dame de Maignelay
2 CONT Strategic Role: Royal Inner-Circle Anchor; responsible for providing the courtly sophistication and Valois connections that solidified the Halluin name within the "Inner Circle" of the French throne.
2 CONT Titles: Duchesse d’Halluin, Marquise de Maignelay.
2 CONT Filiation: Daughter of Philippe de Chabot, Comte de Charny and Admiral of France, and Françoise de Longwy, Dame de Pagny (niece of King Francis I).
2 CONT Active Period (Flourished): c. 1559–1590.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''II. Biographical Sketch: The Historical Context'''
2 CONT Anne-Catherine de Chabot was a woman of "Sovereign Grace" who grew up at the highest levels of the French political hierarchy. Her 1559 marriage to Charles d'Halluin occurred during the pivotal year of the Treaty of Cateau-Cambrés
2 CONC is and served as a centerpiece of aristocratic strategy.
2 CONT
2 CONT As the "Regent of the Halluin Lands," she managed the vast estates of Maignelay during the Wars of Religion, acting with the resilience of a "Grande Dame of the Renaissance". Her presence in the household ensured the 1st Duke's st
2 CONC atus remained "Royal-adjacent," successfully bridging provincial power with the high-court pedigree of the French Peerage.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''III. Heraldry'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Blazon: Or, three chabots (fish) haurient Gules (Chabot); impaled with Argent, three lions rampant sable (Halluin).
2 CONT
2 CONT Heraldic Display: The "speaking arms" of the three red fish on a golden field, when draped under a Duchess’s Mantle and impaled with the black Halluin lions, created one of the most recognizable achievements at court.
2 CONT
2 CONT Heraldic Significance: The inclusion of the Chabot-Brion arms visually codified the merger of the Halluin lineage with the elite "Princes des Fleurs-de-Lys" circles.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''IV. Forensic Correction Log'''
2 CONT '''Finding: The "Brion" Distinction Requirement'''
2 CONT Traditional Claim: Often listed under the general "Chabot" surname common to Poitou and Brittany.
2 CONT
2 CONT Correction: Mandatory identification as Chabot-Brion.
2 CONT
2 CONT Rationale: Essential for distinguishing her specific branch from collateral lines (such as Henri de Chabot) and correctly identifying her as the Admiral's heir.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Finding: Successional Anchor for the 2nd Duchess'''
2 CONT Traditional Claim: Viewed as a standard consort figure.
2 CONT
2 CONT Correction: Re-classified as the Primary Source of Valois Prestige for her daughter, Anne d'Halluin.
2 CONT
2 CONT Rationale: Anne-Catherine’s royal connections through Françoise de Longwy provided the social gravity required for her daughter to inherit the Dukedom suo jure.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''V. Documentation and Evidence (The Auditor’s Trail)'''
2 CONT * Père Anselme, "Histoire Généalogique de la Maison Royale de France" (Vol. IV): Details the specific Chabot-Brion lineage and the marriage contract with Charles.
2 CONT * Archives Nationales (Paris) - Série K (Monuments Historiques): Correspondence concerning the Chabot dowry and the administration of the Maignelay estates.
2 CONT * Brantôme, "Vies des Dames Illustres": Provides a contemporary social context for her role within the Renaissance court.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''VI. User Correction Ledger:'''
2 CONT Explicitly identifies Anne-Catherine as the "Inner-Circle" wing of the project. Her status as a niece-by-marriage to King Francis I is the forensic proof that the Halluin-Piennes line successfully moved from the "French Pivot" to 
2 CONC the apex of the social pyramid.
2 CONT
2 CONT <span style="color:red; font-weight:bold;">DISCLAIMER: This profile is drafted as a Forensic Audit with AI assistance. It prioritizes the "Paper Trail" of the French Royal Household and the Cawley/Warlop standards of evidence over
2 CONC  traditional narratives. (This summary is intended for research leads only; cross-verification with original primary documentation is essential for final lineage certification.)</span>
