2 CONC f-sister of King Francis I of France.
2 CONT
2 CONT At two weeks old her mother, influential in the court of Catherine de'Medici, placed her in the royal convent of Jouarre, near Meaux, to be raised as a nun. The young Charlotte shocked both her family and the royal court by escapi
2 CONC ng the convent in 1572, announcing her conversion to Calvinism and fleeing to the Palatinate, well beyond her parents' reach.
2 CONT
