1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Sir William Shelley, Justice of the Court of Common Pleas & Alice Belknap had 7 sons (including '''John'''; Sir Richard; Sir Edward; Thomas; & Sir James) and 7 daughters (including Katherine, wife of Henry Browne, 
2 CONC Esq; Elizabeth, wife of Sir Roger Copley; Frances; & Margaret, wife of Edward Gage '''(sic: error - Margaret was daughter of John the son, as below)'''.
2 CONT
2 CONT From  [https://books.google.com/books?id=5ikwAAAAYAAJ&lpg=PA68&ots=cDK4nbyZ_J&dq=mary%20wriothesley%20William%20Shelley&pg=PA68#v=twopage&q&f=true Googlebooks] The Baronetage of England: Or The History of the English Baronets, and
2 CONC  Such Baronets of Scotland, as are of English Families; with Genealogical Tables, and Engravings of Their Coats of Arms, Volume 1.  William Betham.  Burrell and Bransby, 1801 - Baronetage.  "Shelley of Michelgrove, Sussex.". Page 
2 CONC 68-69:
2 CONT
2 CONT ==6. John Shelley of Michelgrove, Esq. the eldest son, ==
2 CONT
2 CONT married Mary, daughter of Sir William Fitz-Williams, Knt. and Maud his wife, daughter of Sir Richard Sackvile of Buckhurst, Knt. (who surviving him, married Sir Robert Guldeford, Knt.) by whom he had two sons and six daughters;
2 CONT
2 CONT *1, William, who married to his first wife, Jane, daughter and heir of Lingen of Sutton, in Herefordshire, Esq. and secondly Mary, daughter of Thomas Wriothesley, earl of Southampton, relict of ■ Lister, Esq. son and heir of Sir M
2 CONC artin Lister, Knt. but left no issue. He was attainted for treason, committed Dec. 15, 25 Eliz. whereby his estate was forfeited to the crown during his life, for he did not die till April 15, 39 Eliz. when, by virtue of an entail
2 CONC , the estates both in Sussex and Warwickshire descended to his brother
2 CONT *2, John Shelley, Esq. second son, heir to his mother, married Eleanor, daughter of Sir Thomas Lovell of East-Harling, in Norfolk, Knt. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Of the daughters, 
2 CONT * 1, Elizabeth was married to Sir Thomas Gifford, Knt. 
2 CONT * 2, Eleanor, to Thomas Norton, Esq. son and heir to Sir John Norton of Norwood, in Kent, Knt.  
2 CONT * 3, Margaret to Edward Gage, Esq.  
2 CONT * 4, Mary to Sir George Cotton of Warblington, in Southamptonshire, Knt.  
2 CONT * 5, Bridget married to Sir Anth. Hungerford of Downampney, in Wilts, Knt. and  
2 CONT * '''''6, Anne, wife to Sir Richard Shirley of Wiston, in-Sussex, Knt.''''' (sic: not his daughter)
2 CONT
2 CONT ==comments==
2 CONT
2 CONT Will of John Shelley, Esq, written 5 Oct 1550 (5 Oct. 4 Edward VI) names " ... my 4 daughters Elinor, Mary, Bryget and Margaret ...".  6, [http://www.geni.com/people/Alma-Anne-Shirley/6000000006444364022 Anne Shelley] wife to Sir 
2 CONC Richard Shirley of Wiston, in-Sussex, Knt.  was born about 1500, daughter of [https://www.geni.com/people/John-Shelly/6000000006444777266?through=6000000006444364022 John Shelley, MP] (b 1448) & [https://www.geni.com/people/Elizab
2 CONC eth-Shelley/6000000006444758292?through=6000000006444364022 Elizabeth Michelgrove].  The pedigree appears in error.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==notes==
2 CONT
2 CONT From [http://www.gutenberg.org/files/41747/41747-h/41747-h.htm "The Real Shelley"] Vol. I (of 2), by John Cordy Jeaffreson
2 CONT
2 CONT >Bred to the law, William Shelley (the grandson, or maybe the great-grandson, of the afore-mentioned Member for Rye) became Reader of the Inner Temple in 1517 ... Surviving the sovereign, whom he served on the bench of the Common 
2 CONC Pleas for twenty years, Sir William Shelley served Edward the Sixth in the same capacity, to the day of his own death, which occurred between November 3, 1548 (the date of his last fine), and May 10, 1549, the date of his successo
2 CONC r’s appointment.  Fortunate in his professional career, Sir William Shelley was no less fortunate in his domestic affairs. Marrying an heiress, he had, with other children, John, the grandfather of the first Michelgrove baronet ..
2 CONC .. 
2 CONT
2 CONT A P Baggs, C R J Currie, C R Elrington, S M Keeling and A M Rowland, 'Clapham', in A History of the County of Sussex: Volume 6 Part 1, Bramber Rape (Southern Part), ed. T P Hudson (London, 1980), pp. 10-21 http://www.british-histo
2 CONC ry.ac.uk/vch/sussex/vol6/pt1/pp10-21 [accessed 9 June 2015].
2 CONT
2 CONT >Sir William Shelley, John's son, succeeded in 1527 (fn. 81) and bought Clapham manor in the same year. Thereafter the two manors descended together, Michelgrove eventually becoming absorbed in Clapham. Sir William found favour wi
2 CONC th Henry VIII and was made a judge of Common Pleas and recorder of London. (fn. 82) His brothers Edward and Richard founded the Warminghurst and Patcham branches of the family. (fn. 83) Sir William was succeeded in 1549 (fn. 84) b
2 CONC y '''his son John''' (d. 1550).
2 CONT
2 CONT From http://fortunatusfamilia.com.au/getperson.php?personID=I08544&tree=tree1
2 CONT
2 CONT Will of John Shelley of Michelgrove, Sussex 27 April 1551 PROB 11/34
2 CONT
2 CONT >JOHN SHELLEY, esq. Vol. 94, No. 53. Lewes, 5 Oct. (? 5) Edward VI. Died 4 Edward VI. Heir, son William S., aged 12. Lands in Shepley. J. S., son and heir of "William Shelley, knt., Mary, wife of J. S. and daughter of "Wm. FitzWil
2 CONC liams, knt. J. S. seized of manor of Knell, co. Sussex. Made will 8 Aug. 1550 as J. S. of Mychelgrove, esq. to be buried in Church of Clapham my manor of Stondon Hall, co. Essex, my manors of Wolston and Marston, co. Warwick, Mary
2 CONC  my wife my manor of Chalfyn, co. Herts, my uncle Kychard Shelley's lands in Eudgwicke, my brother Thomas S. and Mary his wife son William under 21 my daughters and younger children my two sons John S. and Eichard S. my manors of 
2 CONC Exton Bassett and Luces in co. Wilts to son Eichard my father S r W m Shelley my 4 daughters Elinor, Mary, Bryget and Margaret my sister Margaret ray uncle parson Shelley my uncle Edward Shelley.
2 CONT
2 CONT >WILLIAM SHELLEY, esq. Vol. 124, No. 164. (Proof of age.) Clapham, 19 Sept. 1 Elizabeth. Jurors state that W. S., son and heir of John Shelley, esq., deceased, is aged 21 years and 5 days on this date.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
