2 CONT * Sir William Shelley (1480?–1549) was an English judge.
2 CONT *Born about 1480, he was the eldest son of Sir John Shelley (died 3 Jan. 1526) and his wife Elizabeth (died 31 July 1513), daughter and heir of John de Michelgrove in the parish of Clapham, Sussex. Of the judge's six brothers ....
2 CONC  etc.
2 CONT *Shelley married Alice (died 1536?), daughter of Sir Henry Belknap, grandson of Sir Robert de Bealknap of Knelle in the parish of Beckley, Sussex. By her he had four sons:
2 CONT **''' John (died 15 December 1550), father of William (not the same person as William Shelley of Hertford, also a prisoner in the Tower in 1580), who was attainted 15 December 1582 for complicity in Charles Paget's treasons, but n
2 CONC ot executed, and died 15 April 1597, being succeeded by his son John, created a baronet in 1611;
2 CONT ** Sir Richard Shelley;
2 CONT ** the third son, Sir James, was, like Sir Richard, a distinguished and widely travelled Knight of St. John;
2 CONT ** the fourth, Sir Edward, was a master of the household of Henry VIII, treasurer of the council of the north, and captain of Berwick, and was killed at the battle of Pinkie on 10 September 1547.
2 CONT *Their daughter Elizabeth married Roger Copley, father of Sir Thomas Copley.[2]
2 CONT *From: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sir_William_Shelley ____________________________________
2 CONT *'''Dictionary of National Biography: From the Earliest Times to 1900 (1897) Vol. 52
2 CONT *https://archive.org/details/dictionarynatio01leegoog
2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/dictionarynatio01leegoog#page/n59/mode/1up
2 CONT *Pg.41
2 CONT *   SHELLEY, SIR WILLIAM (1480?-1549?), judge, born about 1480, was the eldest son of Sir John Shelley (d. 3 Jan. 1526) and his wife Elizabeth (d. 31 July 1513), daughter and heir of John de Michelgrove in the parish of Clapham, S
2 CONC ussex (reproductions of monumental brasses in Addit. MS. 32490). .... etc.
2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/dictionarynatio01leegoog#page/n60/mode/1up
2 CONT *Pg.42
2 CONT * .... He died between 3 Nov. 1548 and 10 May 1549.
2 CONT *   Shelley married Alice (d. 1536?), daughter of Sir Henry Belknap, great-grandson of Sir Robert de Bealknap [q. v.] of Knelle in the parish of Beckley, Sussex. By her he had four sons: '''John (d. 15 Dec. 1550) was father of Wil
2 CONC liam (not be confused with William Shelley of Hertford, also a prisoner in the Tower in 1580), who was attainted 15 Dec. 1582 for complicity in Charles Paget's treasons, but not executed, and died 15 April 1597, being succeeded by
2 CONC  his son''' John, created a baronet in 1611; the second son of the judge was Sir Richard Shelley [q. v.]; the third, Sir James, was, like Sir Richard, a distinquished and widely travelled knight of St. John (cf. Notes and Queries,
2 CONC  1st ser. viii. 192, x. 201-2); the fourth, Sir Edward, a master of the household of Henry VIII, treasurer of the council of the north, and captain of Berwick, was killed at Pinkie on 10 Sept. 1547 (cf. Addit. MSS. 32647 ff. 66, 7
2 CONC 0, 32648 f. 12, 32653 f. 161; Chron. of Calais, p. 176, &c.; Lit. Rem. of Edward VI, Rosb. Club, pp. cc; Cal. Hamilton Papers, passim). .... etc. _________________________
2 CONT *Links
2 CONT * http://www.historyofparliamentonline.org/volume/1509-1558/member/shelley-william-1479-1549
2 CONT * http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Shelley,_William_(1480%3F-1549%3F)_(DNB00)
2 CONT
