1 NAME Alice /Shirley/
2 GIVN Alice
2 SURN Shirley
2 _MARNM Chaloner
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1506
2 ADDR
3 CITY Westneston (now Wiston)
3 STAE England
1 DEAT
2 DATE BEF 9 MAY 1570
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Alice Shirley (b abt 1506 - Buried: 9 May 1570) was the daughter of Sir Richard Shirley of Wiston, Sussex  (Bef 1477-1540) and Alma Shelley  (-Abt 1542).
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family
2 CONT
2 CONT https://buist-keatch.org/buist/goring/2530.html
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Marriage (1): Thomas Chaloner of Lindfield, Sussex about 1527.  He was the son of John Chaloner of Lindfield, Sussex  (-Bef 1521) and Alice  (-Bef 1521).
2 CONT
2 CONT Their children  
2 CONT
2 CONT # John Chaloner Born: Abt 1534 Died: 7 May 1578 aged about 44
2 CONT # Richard Chaloner Born: Abt 1536
2 CONT # Francis Chaloner Born: Abt 1537
2 CONT # Thomas Chaloner Born: Abt 1538 Died: Oct 1587 aged about 49
2 CONT # Jane Chaloner married Maurice Tichborne of Cowden, Kent.
2 CONT # Dorothy Chaloner married John Tichborne of Cowden, Kent
2 CONT # Mary Chaloner married George de Holand of Angmering, Sussex
2 CONT # Margaret Chaloner Marriage (1): William Courthope, Marriage (2): Richard Mill, Marriage (3): Sir William Goring of Burton, Sussex
2 CONT # Chaloner Born: Abt 1548
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Origins 
2 CONT
2 CONT Stemmata Shirleiana.  By E.P. Shirley.  Page 246. [https://books.google.com/books?id=_vQRAwAAQBAJ&lpg=PP1&vq=Chaloner&pg=PA246#v=twopage&q=Lindfield&f=false GoogleBooks]
2 CONT
2 CONT By his first wife Sir Richard had issue four sons and six daughters: viz.
2 CONT William Sherley his eldest son, Thomas, Edward, and Richard; of the three younger sons I have no further accounts; the daughters were,
2 CONT * 1. Elizabeth, who married John Mychell of Stammerham, in the parish of Horsham, in Sussex, esq.
2 CONT * 2. '''Alice, married Thomas Challenor of Kenwardes in Lindfield, in Sussex, esq'''.
2 CONT * 3. Anne, married Richard Earnfold of Wickham, in the parish of Steyning, in Sussex, esq.
2 CONT * 4. Cecilia, married Richard Leeds of Steyning (?) in Sussex, esq.
2 CONT * 5, 6. Jane and Frances were the other two daughters, who appear to have died unmarried
2 CONT
2 CONT ==notes==
2 CONT (A different) Alice Shirley Chaloner‘s daughter Mary Chaloner’s husband John Cowper is listed in her brother Ralph Sherley of Wiston Will, proved in 1510:
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Will of Ralph Sherley of Wiston Esq. 1510 - 11 Feb 1509. To be buried in church of Westneston, to Cathedral of Chichester, to church of Westneston, chapel of Heene, church of Chiltyngton, church of Chesham Wobone Bucks, church of 
2 CONC Lytelmyssyngdon, church of Lynemynster, church of Stenyning, Ffyndon, Wasshyngton, Ashynton, Bownton (Buncton), Ashurst, Botolphs, Cokeham, Lawnsyng and Olde Shorym. To daughter Jahane Dawtre, Elizbeth Lee, Beatrix Elryngton, and 
2 CONC Isabell Dawtre, to Rauff Belyngham the younger and Rauff Palmer my godchildren, to nephew Andrew Tanner, to Edward Berde, to wife Johane farm of Bodyngton, to son Thomas Sherley, to son Richard. Wife executor, to good friend and c
2 CONC ousin John Sherley cofferer to the King overseer, "where Thos Cooke, Rauff Belyngham, John Lee, Edward Palmer, '''John Cowper''' and Wingary Sayne lately recovered against me certain lands and tenements in Hunderage, Charlerage, B
2 CONC otley, Chesham Leycester, and Chesham Wobourn in county of Buckinghamshire the use of me during my life…PCC Proven 1510.
2 CONT
2 CONT Stirnet's "Shirley1" page (link below) does not mention that Alice's marriage or issue.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Chaloner-31
2 CONT
2 CONT “Mary who married John Cowper was Not the daughter of Thomas Chaloner and his wife Alice. Although Thomas had a daughter named Mary, she was still unmarried in his will of 1559. [2]“
2 CONT
