2 CONC  a low-point in 1600, when Maurice dismissed him as lieutenant-general of Holland and Zeeland.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1604 Hohenlohe became ill and started getting paralysis-symptoms. In 1606 he died. After his death his body was taken to Öhringen (Baden-Württemberg) by his wife, and he was interred in the family-tomb in the collegiate church 
2 CONC of St. Peter and St. Paul.
