1 OCCU Duchess Consort of Bavaria
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Anna of Austria (Prague, July 7, 1528 – Munich, October 16, 1590) was the daughter of Ferdinand I, Holy Roman Emperor and his wife Anna of Bohemia and Hungary (1503–1547).
2 CONT
2 CONT She was engaged several times as a child, first to Prince Theodor of Bavaria (1526–1534), then to Charles of Orleans (1522–1545), but both died young.
2 CONT
2 CONT Anna finally married on July 4, 1546 in Regensburg at the age of 17 , Duke Albert V, Duke of Bavaria, the brother of her first fiancé. The wedding gift was 50,000 Guilder. The couple lived at the Trausnitz Castle in Landshut, unti
2 CONC l Albert became Duke.
2 CONT
2 CONT Anna and Albert had great influence on the spiritual life in the Duchy, and enhanced the reputation of Munchen as a city of art, by founding several musea and the Bayerischen Staatsbibliothek.
2 CONT
2 CONT Anna and Albert were also patrons to the painter Hans Müelich, and composer Orlando di Lasso.
2 CONT
2 CONT Karl (7 September 1547 – 7 December 1547) 
2 CONT
2 CONT William V (1548–1626) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Ferdinand (20 January 1550 – 30 January 1608) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Maria Anna (1551–1608) married Archduke Charles II of Austria 
2 CONT
2 CONT Maximiliana Maria (4 July 1552 – 11 July 1614) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Friedrich (26 July 1553 – 18 April 1554) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Ernst (17 December 1554 – 17 February 1612), Archbishop of Cologne 
