1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Barbara_of_Austria '''Barbara von Österreich-Habsburg''']
2 CONT
2 CONT Archduchess Barbara of Austria
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT   (Redirected from Barbara of Austria)
2 CONT
2 CONT Jump to:navigation, search
2 CONT
2 CONT Barbara of Austria
2 CONT
2 CONT Barbara of Austria (30 April 1539 – 19 September 1572) was born in Vienna to Ferdinand I, Holy Roman Emperor and Anna of Bohemia and Hungary. From 1547, in Innsbruck with her sisters Magdalena, Margareta, Helena and Johanna, she r
2 CONC eceived a deeply religious upbringing.
2 CONT
2 CONT Even though Barbara was regarded as ugly, several marriage proposals had been made. In 1565 her marriage to Alfonso II, Duke of Ferrara, was celebrated with much splendour. It was a happy marriage but it remained childless. Torqua
2 CONC to Tasso who, in 1565, had been called to the court of Ferrara, dedicated some sonnets to her.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1570 and 1571, after an earthquake, using her own income she supported young girls without parents. She founded the Conservatore delle orfane di Santa Barbara which was very much appreciated by the population of Ferrara. She wa
2 CONC s in constant touch with the Jesuits but also had a very close relationship with her Protestant mother-in-law, Renée of France, daughter of Louis XII of France.
2 CONT
2 CONT Having been sickly since 1566, she died, aged thirty-three, of tuberculosis on 19 September 1572.
2 CONT
