2 CONT Maria Manuela, Princess of Portugal (1527–1545; Portuguese pronunciation: [mɐˈɾiɐ mɐnuˈɛlɐ]; English: Mary Emmanuella) was a daughter of King John III of Portugal and his wife Catherine of Habsburg. She was Princess of Asturias as
2 CONC  spouse of Philip, Prince of Asturias, and between 1527 and 1535 Princess of Portugal in her own right.
2 CONT
2 CONT Maria was born in Coimbra on 15 October 1527 and was one of the few children of John III to survive childhood. She married her double-cousin Prince Philip of Asturias (future Philip II of Spain and I of Portugal) and was the mothe
2 CONC r of Prince Carlos, a deformed child who was heir of the Spanish crown.
2 CONT
2 CONT Maria died soon after she gave birth to Don Carlos of Spain (1545–1568) on 12 August 1545 in Valladolid, Spain.
