1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Kilmarnock, industrial town, East Ayrshire council area, historic county of Ayrshire, southwestern Scotland. 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===MARGARET STEWART===
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret Stewart is the bastard daughter of James IV, King of Scots, and Margaret Drummond. [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun01paul/page/22/mode/1up The Scots Peerage I: 22]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret Stewart, daughter of James IV King of Scots and Margaret Drummond (a), married, as her 3rd husband, her 2nd cousin, Sir John Drummond, III.  They had the same Grandfather, Sir John Drummond, I. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret Stewart was born illegitimately circa 1497.1 She married, firstly, John Gordon, Lord Gordon, son of Alexander Gordon, 3rd Earl of Huntly and Lady Jean Stewart, in November 1512.2 She married, secondly, Sir John Drummond o
2 CONC f Innerpeffray on 20 January 1530/31.2
2 CONT
2 CONT She was the daughter of James IV, King of Scots and Margaret Drummond.1 From November 1512, her married name became Gordon.2 From 20 January 1530/31, her married name became Drummond.2
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Margaret Stewart and Sir John Drummond of Innerpeffray
2 CONT
2 CONT ># Agnes Drummond+3 d. 21 Jan 1589/90
2 CONT ># Margaret Drummond+
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Margaret Stewart and John Gordon, Lord Gordon
2 CONT
2 CONT ># Alexander Gordon2
2 CONT ># James Gordon4
2 CONT ># George Gordon, 4th Earl of Huntly+2 b. 1513, d. 22 Oct 1562
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT #     [S11] Alison Weir, Britain's Royal Family: A Complete Genealogy (London, U.K.: The Bodley Head, 1999), page 240. Hereinafter cited as Britain's Royal Family.
2 CONT #     [S37] Charles Mosley, editor, Burke's Peerage, Baronetage & Knightage, 107th edition, 3 volumes (Wilmington, Delaware, U.S.A.: Burke's Peerage (Genealogical Books) Ltd, 2003), volume 2, page 2011. Hereinafter cited as Burke'
2 CONC s Peerage and Baronetage, 107th edition.
2 CONT #     [S6] G.E. Cokayne; with Vicary Gibbs, H.A. Doubleday, Geoffrey H. White, Duncan Warrand and Lord Howard de Walden, editors, The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain and the United Kingdom, Extant, Ex
2 CONC tinct or Dormant, new ed., 13 volumes in 14 (1910-1959; reprint in 6 volumes, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 2000), volume XI, page 624. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Peerage.
2 CONT #     [S37] Charles Mosley, Burke's Peerage and Baronetage, 107th edition, volume 2, page 2012.
