2 CONT Sophie of Schleswig-Holstein-Gottorp
2 CONT
2 CONT Duchess Sophia of Mecklenburg-Schwerin
2 CONT
2 CONT Sophie of Schleswig-Holstein-Gottorp ( June 1 1569 in Gottorp , † November 14th 1634 in Schwerin ) was 1603-1608 de facto regent of the duchy of Mecklenburg-Schwerin .
2 CONT
2 CONT [ edit ] Life
2 CONT
2 CONT Sophia was the eldest daughter of the Duke Adolf I of Holstein-Gottorp and his wife Christine of Hesse . She married on 17 February 1588 in Reinbek Duke Johann VII of Mecklenburg . John was regarded as a weak ruler who understood 
2 CONC not to rule his indebted and corrupt country. Sophia lived in almost poverty. Her husband stabbed himself in 1592 with seven stab wounds, and even took over first Duke Ulrich of Mecklenburg the regency. Sophia went on her widow's 
2 CONC seat in Lübz back, while the country by the administrators of Duke Ulrich increasingly dilapidated.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sophia managed the lands of her jointure , the offices Rehna and Wittenburg very carefully, sparingly and carefully. After the death of Ulrich Herzog 1603, Herzog was Charles of Mecklenburg Schwerin in Regent part of the country, 
2 CONC entrusted with the task of Sophia, her sons to manage the inheritance. She walked vigorously against the abuses of the previous administration. 1608 could be explained Duke Karl Sophia's eldest son by the emperor for age. Sophia's
2 CONC  sons had been some time estranged from her mother again and provided for a financial breakdown of the Land's, which had ordered the mother to some extent.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Dowager Duchess moved again back to Lübz. Their goods were of Wallenstein guaranteed, even if their sons in 1628 after the imperial had to leave the country.
2 CONT
2 CONT By Sophia origin of the two lines later the Grand Duchy of Mecklenburg-Schwerin and Mecklenburg-Strelitz from.
2 CONT
