2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret of Austria (1584-1611)
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret of Austria (December 25, 1584-October 3, 1611), Queen of Spain and Portugal, was the daughter of Archduke Charles II of Austria and Maria Anna of Bavaria, and the sister of the Emperor Ferdinand II.
2 CONT
2 CONT She married Philip III of Spain on 18 April 1599. Margaret was a great patroness of the arts. She was very influential in palace life.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was the mother of:
2 CONT
2 CONT Anne of Austria (1601 - 1666), who became Queen of France; wife of King Louis XIII of France.
2 CONT
2 CONT Philip IV of Spain (1605 - 1665) Married Elisabeth of Bourbon sister of Louis XIII of France.
2 CONT
2 CONT Maria Ana of Spain (1606 - 1646).
2 CONT
2 CONT Cardinal-Infante Ferdinand (1609/1610 - 1641). He became Governor of the Habsburg Netherlands.
