2 CONT http://genealogy.euweb.cz/hung/zrinyi.html http://hr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Knezovi_Zrinski http://hr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Juraj_IV._Zrinski http://hu.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zr%C3%ADnyi_csal%C3%A1d http://hu.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zr%C3%ADnyi_V
2 CONC I._Mikl%C3%B3s http://hu.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zr%C3%ADnyi_Gy%C3%B6rgy_(t%C3%A1rnokmester) http://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Juraj_(IV.)_Zrinski
2 CONT
2 CONT '''VI. Nicholas Zrinyi according the Wikipedia articles from his family and his father and himself (even in the same language) are contradictory.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT The article on Croatian-language from his family his birth year ca. 1570 (date of birth in the Hungarian article contains no data) both article (and EuWeb too) labeled his mother was Anna D'Arco 
2 CONT
2 CONT From himself both articles states he born from his father’s second marriage, but in the German article is contrary. Neither the year of birth, or the mother of VI. Nicholas could not find in the Croatian article, but in the Hungar
2 CONC ian article his birthdate was the 1580's and clearly states that VI. Nicholaus was the eldest son of V. George and Sophie Countess Stubenberg.
2 CONT
