2 CONT Alfonsos Ehefrau Isabella von Savoyen
2 CONT
2 CONT Alfonso III. d’Este (* 22. Oktober 1591 in Ferrara; † 24. Mai 1644 in Castelnovo di Garfagnana, Capri) war der älteste Sohn des Herzogs Cesare d’Este von Modena und Reggio und wurde nach dessen Tod am 11. Dezember 1628 sein Nachfo
2 CONC lger. Er trat bereits ein halbes Jahr später, am 25. Juli 1629, zugunsten seines Sohnes Francesco I. d’Este zurück.
2 CONT
2 CONT Er heiratete am 22. Februar 1608 Isabella von Savoyen (* 11. März 1591; † 22. August 1626) Tochter des Herzogs Emanuele I. Das Paar hatte 14 Kinder:
2 CONT
2 CONT    1. Cesare d’Este (* 1609; † 1613)
2 CONT
2 CONT    2. Francesco I. d’Este (1610–1658) Herzog 1629 ∞ 1) 1631 Maria Farnese (1615–1646) Tochter des Ranuccio I. Farnese Herzog von Parma, ∞ 2) 1648 Vittoria Farnese (1618–1649), deren Schwester, ∞ 3) 1654 Lucrezia Barberini (1630–16
2 CONC 99), Tochter des Taddeo
2 CONT
2 CONT    3. Obizzo d’Este (* 1611; † 24. August 1645), Bischof von Modena 1640
2 CONT
2 CONT    4. Caterina d’Este (* 2. Februar 1613; † 1635), Nonne
2 CONT
2 CONT    5. Cesare d’Este (* 1614; † 20. September 1677)
2 CONT
2 CONT    6. Alessandro d’Este (*/† 1615)
2 CONT
2 CONT    7. Carlo Alessandro d’Este (* 1616; † 1679)
2 CONT
2 CONT    8. Rinaldo d’Este (* 1618; † 30. Oktober 1671), Kardinal 1641
2 CONT
2 CONT    9. Margherita d’Este (* 1619; † 12. November 1692) ∞ 23. Juni 1647 Ferrante III. Gonzaga, Herzog von Guastalla (1618–1678)
2 CONT
2 CONT   10. Beatrice d’Este (*/† 1620)
2 CONT
2 CONT   11. Beatrice d’Este (* 1622; † 1623)
2 CONT
2 CONT   12. Filiberto d’Este (* 1623; † 1645)
2 CONT
2 CONT   13. Bonifazio d’Este (*/† 1624)
2 CONT
2 CONT   14. Anna Beatrice d’Este (* 1626; † 25. September 1690) ∞ 29. April 1656 Alessandro II. Pico, Herzog von Mirandola (* 30. März 1631; † 3. Februar 1691)
2 CONT
2 CONT Vorgänger
2 CONT
2 CONT Cesare
2 CONT
2 CONT 	Herzog von Modena und Reggio
2 CONT
2 CONT 1628–1629 	Nachfolger
2 CONT
2 CONT Francesco I.
2 CONT
2 CONT Normdaten: PND: 119228106 – weitere Informationen
2 CONT
2 CONT Diese Seite wurde zuletzt am 1. Juni 2010 um 15:59 Uhr geändert.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Alfonso III d'Este (22 October 1591 - 26 May 1644) was Duke of Modena and Reggio from 1628 to 1629. He was the husband of Princess Isabella of Savoy, daughter of Charles Emmanuel I, Duke of Savoy and his wife Infanta Catherine Mic
2 CONC helle of Spain. [edit] Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Born in Ferrara, he was the son of Cesare d'Este, Duke of Modena and Virginia de' Medici. In 1613 he took part in the war against Lucca and had a primary role in the assassination of count Ercole Pepoli, who was disputing the duch
2 CONC y with Cesare, at Ferrara (1617).
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1608 he was married to Isabella of Savoy, daughter of Charles Emmanuel I of Savoy. Profoundly in love with her, when she died in 1626 he started to think to take religious vows. When his father died in 1628, Alfonso became Duke
2 CONC  of Modena and Reggio. However, in July 1629 he announced his abdication from the Castle of Sassuolo. On September 8 of the same year he entered the Capuchin friars under the name of fra' Giambattista da Modena.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was distinguished as a preacher and helper of dying people during the pestilence which struck the Duchy in 1630-1631. In the following year he returned to Modena, but his discourses against the costumes of the court made him un
2 CONC welcome, so he retired to a convent in Castelnuovo di Garfagnana, built by his son, Duke Francesco I, where he died in 1644.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.familysearch.org/en/tree/person/details/L45Q-W4Y
