1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] Children
1 CONT
1 CONT Charles married Marie of Anjou on 18 December 1422. Their children include:
1 CONT
1 CONT     * Louis XI, King of France (1423–83)
1 CONT     * John of France (1424-25)
1 CONT     * Radegonde de France (1428–44)
1 CONT     * Catherine (1428-1446), married Charles de Charolais, future Charles le Téméraire, Duke of Burgundy, in 1440
1 CONT     * Jacques de France (1432-1437)
1 CONT     * Yolande de France (1434–78), married the future Amadeus IX, Duke of Savoy in 1452. Upon his death in 1472, she became regent of Savoy.
1 CONT     * Joan (1435–82), married the future John II, Duke of Bourbon in 1452
1 CONT     * Margaret of France (1437–38)
1 CONT     * Mary of France (7 September 1438 – 14 February 1439)
1 CONT     * Jeanne (7 September 1438 – 26 December 1446)
1 CONT     * Magdalena of Valois (1443–86), married Gaston de Foix, prince de Viane, in 1462
1 CONT     * Charles, Duc de Berry (1446–72)
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] Mistresses
1 CONT
1 CONT     * Odette de Champdivers — formerly mistress to Charles VII's uncle Louis of Valois, Duke of Orleans and his father Charles VI of France.
1 CONT     * Agnès Sorel.
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] Charles VII in the Arts
1 CONT
1 CONT     * Appears as Charles the Dauphin in George Bernard Shaw's play Saint Joan
1 CONT     * Appears as the Dauphin in William Shakespeare's play "Henry V"
1 CONT     * Appears as a significant character in Thomas Keneally's novel "Blood Red, Sister Rose".
1 CONT     * Two Russian operas from the late 19th century portray Charles VII (and Agnès Sorel) among the dramatis personæ. These are Pyotr Tchaikovsky's The Maid of Orleans and César Cui's The Saracen.
1 CONT     * Charles VII has been represented in the movies by Raymond Hatton (1917), Jean Debucourt (1929), Gustaf Gründgens (1935), Emlyn Williams (1935), Max Adrian (1944), José Ferrer (1948), Paul Colline (1955), Richard Widmark (195
1 CONC 7), Daniel Gélin (1978), Keith Drinkel (1979), Oleg Kulko (1993), John Malkovich (1999), Neil Patrick Harris (1999)
