0 @N6000000002188309357@ NOTE Edmund Tudor, 1st Earl of Richmond
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Edmund Tudor, 1st Earl of Richmond (c. 1430 – November 1, 1456) was the father of King Henry VII of England.
1 CONT
1 CONT Tudor was born either at Much Hadham Palace in Hertfordshire or at Hadham in Bedfordshire, an older son of Owen Tudor and Catherine of Valois (former wife of King Henry V of England). It is not known for certain whether he was bor
1 CONC n legitimately after his parents were secretly married. Whatever the case, his mother died in 1437, but his half-brother King Henry VI recognised him and elevated him as Earl of Richmond in November 1452. Edmund's younger brother,
1 CONC  Jasper, was created Earl of Pembroke.
1 CONT
1 CONT On 1 November 1455, he married Lady Margaret Beaufort, a daughter of the legitimised John Beaufort, 1st Duke of Somerset. She was twelve years old at the time, and became pregnant in the following year. However, during the opening
1 CONC  rounds of the Wars of the Roses, Edmund was captured by the Yorkist Herbert family. They imprisoned him at Carmarthen Castle in south Wales, where he caught the plague and died. Henry, his only child, was born at Pembroke Castle,
1 CONC  only two months after his death.
1 CONT Preceded by
1 CONT John of Lancaster Earl of Richmond
1 CONT 1435-1456 Succeeded by
1 CONT Forfeit, next held by George of Clarence
