1 CONT    Mary, Queen of France
1 CONT    Edmund, Duke of Somerset
1 CONT
1 CONT Arthur Tudor (19 September/20 September 1486–2 April 1502) was the first son of King Henry VII of England and Elizabeth of York, and therefore, heir to the throne of England and Wales. As he predeceased his father he never became 
1 CONC king, and his place was taken by his brother, who became King Henry VIII.
1 CONT Contents
1 CONT [hide]
1 CONT
1 CONT     * 1 Early life
1 CONT           o 1.1 Birth
1 CONT           o 1.2 Betrothal and alliance
1 CONT           o 1.3 Childhood
1 CONT     * 2 Marriage
1 CONT     * 3 Death and aftermath
1 CONT     * 4 Funeral
1 CONT     * 5 Question of consummation
