0 @N6000000002322350435@ NOTE Between 1529 & 1536, the Angilican Church of England was recognized as a
1 CONT a national church independent of papal jurisdiction. Henry VIII, vexed at the
1 CONT refusal of Pope Clement VII to annul his marriage to Catherine of Aragon,
1 CONT induced Parliament to inact a series of statutes denying the Pope any power
1 CONT or jurisdiction over the Church of England. Sadly, even with 6 wives and 3
1 CONT children who would become 1 King and 2 Queens, there were no further direct
1 CONT descendants leading back to Henry VIII.
0 @N6000000002188342076@ NOTE Henry VIII of England
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Henry VIII
1 CONT King of England; King of Ireland (more...)
1 CONT Reign 21 April 1509 – 28 January 1547
1 CONT Coronation 23 June 1509
