1 CONT
1 CONT Edmund Tudor, Duke of Somerset (February 21, 1499 Greenwich Palace – June 19, 1500) was the sixth child of Henry VII of England and Elizabeth of York. He was bestowed at birth with the title Duke of Somerset. He died at 15 months 
1 CONC of unknown causes, and was buried at Westminster Abbey.
1 CONT
1 CONT Edmund's elder siblings (by order of birth) were Arthur, Prince of Wales, Margaret Tudor, Henry VIII of England, Elizabeth Tudor and Mary Tudor, Queen consort of France. His only younger sibling was Catherine Tudor.
