0 @N6000000002187780904@ NOTE James Stewart, Duke of Ross
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT James Stewart, Duke of Ross (March 1476 - January 1504) was the son of King James III of Scotland and Margaret of Denmark. He was made Marquess of Ormonde at his baptism, Earl of Ross in 1481, and Duke of Ross in 1488.
1 CONT
1 CONT Stewart became Archbishop of St. Andrews in 1497 and Lord Chancellor of Scotland in 1502.
1 CONT
1 CONT Stewart had two brothers, King James IV of Scotland and John Stewart, Earl of Mar. It seems surprising that there were two brothers both called James; it has been suggested that at the time the younger was born the older was serio
1 CONC usly ill and seemed unlikely to survive, but it is unclear whether there is any evidence for this hypothesis.
1 CONT
1 CONT Religious Posts 
1 CONT Preceded by:
1 CONT William Scheves Archbishop of St. Andrews
1 CONT 1497–1504 Succeeded by:
1 CONT Alexander Stewart 
1 CONT Preceded by:
1 CONT George Crichton Commendator of Dunfermline
1 CONT 1500–1504 Succeeded by:
1 CONT James Beaton *
1 CONT *His immediate successor may have been Gilbert Strachan. 
1 CONT Political offices 
1 CONT Preceded by:
1 CONT George Gordon, 2nd Earl of Huntly Lord Chancellor of Scotland
1 CONT 1502–1504 Succeeded by:
1 CONT Alexander Stewart 
