1 CONT Fiction
1 CONT
1 CONT     * The short appearance of the future Queen Mary in Mark Twain's The Prince and the Pauper had a considerable influence on her negative image, given the enduring popularity of Twain's work. His depiction of her as a cold and cr
1 CONC uel person seems to connected both to Twain's outspoken atheism and to the strong anti-Catholic prejudice prevalent in American society at the time of writing.
